return {
  ["creature.githyanki-knight.xmm2024"]={title="Githyanki Knight",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 117 (18d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nMisty Step (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githyanki makes three Silver Sword attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB if available.\n\nSilver Sword\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) Psychic damage. Critical hIf the target is in an astral body (as with the XPHB spell), the githyanki can cut the silvery cord that tethers the target to its material body instead of dealing damage."},
  ["creature.githyanki-star-seer.bam2014"]={title="Githyanki Star Seer",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 110 (17d8 + 34)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 19 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githyanki makes three Astral Bolt attacks.\n\nAstral Bolt\n\nms,rs 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h20 (3d10 + 4) radiant damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAstral Step {@recharge 4}\n\nThe githyanki teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.githyanki-supreme-commander.mpmm2014"]={title="Githyanki Supreme Commander",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 187 (22d8 + 88)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 17 | CON 18 | INT 16 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the githyanki fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githyanki makes two Silver Greatsword attacks.\n\nSilver Greatsword\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage plus 17 (5d6) psychic damage. On a critical hit against a target in an astral body (as with the astral projection spell), the githyanki can cut the silvery cord that tethers the target to its material body, instead of dealing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAstral Step\n\nThe githyanki teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe githyanki adds 5 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the githyanki must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCommand Ally\n\nThe githyanki targets one ally it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see or hear the githyanki, the target can make one melee weapon attack using its reaction, if available, and has advantage on the attack roll.\n\nAttack (2 Actions)\n\nThe githyanki makes one Silver Greatsword attack."},
  ["creature.githyanki-supreme-commander.mtf2014"]={title="Githyanki Supreme Commander",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 187 (22d8 + 88)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 17 | CON 18 | INT 16 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githyanki makes two greatsword attacks.\n\nSilver Greatsword\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage plus 17 (5d6) psychic damage. On a critical hit against a target in an astral body (as with the astral projection spell), the githyanki can cut the silvery cord that tethers the target to its material body, instead of dealing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe githyanki adds 5 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the githyanki must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack (2 Actions)\n\nThe githyanki makes a greatsword attack.\n\nCommand Ally\n\nThe githyanki targets one ally it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see or hear the githyanki, the target can make one melee weapon attack using its reaction and has advantage on the attack roll.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe githyanki magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing and carrying, to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of it. It also becomes insubstantial until the start of its next turn. While insubstantial, it can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. If it ends its turn inside an object, it takes 16 (3d10) force damage and is moved to the nearest unoccupied space."},
  ["creature.githyanki-warrior.mm2014"]={title="Githyanki Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 160\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githyanki makes two greatsword attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage."},
  ["creature.githyanki-warrior.xmm2024"]={title="Githyanki Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 134\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nMisty Step (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githyanki makes two Psi Blade attacks.\n\nPsi Blade\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h9 (2d6 + 2) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Psychic damage."},
  ["creature.githyanki-xenomancer.bam2014"]={title="Githyanki Xenomancer",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 157 (21d8 + 63)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 18 | CON 17 | INT 15 | WIS 18 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith plus any four languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githyanki makes three Staff attacks, three Telekinetic Bolt attacks, or a combination thereof.\n\nStaff\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage when used with two hands, plus 14 (4d6) psychic damage.\n\nTelekinetic Bolt\n\nrs 8 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h20 (3d10 + 4) force damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAstral Step {@recharge 4}\n\nThe githyanki teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["species.githzerai.mpmm2014"]={title="Githzerai",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nGithzerai Psionics\n\nYou know the mage hand cantrip, and the hand is invisible when you cast the cantrip with this trait.\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you can cast the shield spell with this trait. Starting at 5th level, you can also cast the detect thoughts spell with it. Once you cast shield or detect thoughts spell with this trait, you can't cast that spell with it again until you finish a long rest. You can also cast either of those spells using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level.\n\nIntelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells when you cast them with this trait (choose when you select this race). None of these spells require spell components when you cast them with this trait.\n\nMental Discipline\n\nYour innate psychic defenses grant you advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the charmed and frightened conditions on yourself.\n\nPsychic Resilience\n\nYou have resistance to psychic damage."},
  ["creature.githzerai-anarch.mpmm2014"]={title="Githzerai Anarch",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 144 (17d8 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 21 | CON 18 | INT 18 | WIS 20 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the githzerai fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes three Unarmed Strike attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nStrike\n\nThe githzerai makes one Unarmed Strike attack.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe githzerai teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of it.\n\nChange Gravity (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe githzerai casts the reverse gravity spell, using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability. The spell has the normal effect, except that the githzerai can orient the area in any direction and creatures and objects fall toward the end of the area."},
  ["creature.githzerai-anarch.mtf2014"]={title="Githzerai Anarch",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 207\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 144 (17d8 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 21 | CON 18 | INT 18 | WIS 20 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the anarch is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe anarch makes three unarmed strikes.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nStrike\n\nThe anarch makes one unarmed strike.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe anarch magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing and carrying, to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of it.\n\nChange Gravity (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe anarch casts the reverse gravity spell. The spell has the normal effect, except that the anarch can orient the area in any direction and creatures and objects fall toward the end of the area."},
  ["creature.githzerai-enlightened.mpmm2014"]={title="Githzerai Enlightened",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 143\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 19 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 19 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes three Unarmed Strike attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) psychic damage.\n\nTemporal Strike {@recharge}\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 52 (8d12) psychic damage. The target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or move 1 round forward in time. A target moved forward in time vanishes for the duration. When the effect ends, the target reappears in the space it left or in an unoccupied space nearest to that space if it's occupied.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSlow Fall\n\nWhen the githzerai falls, it reduces any falling damage it takes by 50."},
  ["creature.githzerai-enlightened.mtf2014"]={title="Githzerai Enlightened",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 19 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 19 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes three unarmed strikes.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 13 (3d8) psychic damage.\n\nTemporal Strike {@recharge}\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 52 (8d12) psychic damage. The target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or move 1 round forward in time. A target moved forward in time vanishes for the duration. When the effect ends, the target reappears in the space it left or in an unoccupied space nearest to that space if it's occupied."},
  ["creature.githzerai-futurist.mpp2014"]={title="Githzerai Futurist",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 149 (23d8 + 46)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 17 | CON 15 | INT 17 | WIS 17 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes three Unarmed Strike or Psychic Bolt attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 11 (2d10) psychic damage.\n\nPsychic Bolt\n\nrs 7 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h21 (4d8 + 3) psychic damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFuture Insight (3/Day)\n\nWhen the githzerai or a creature it can see makes an attack roll, a saving throw, or an ability check, the githzerai can cause the roll to be made with advantage or disadvantage."},
  ["creature.githzerai-monk.mm2014"]={title="Githzerai Monk",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 161\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes two unarmed strikes.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) psychic damage. This is a magic weapon attack."},
  ["creature.githzerai-monk.xmm2024"]={title="Githzerai Monk",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 136\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nPsi-Powered Leap (2/Day)\n\nPsionic Defense (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes two Psi Strike attacks.\n\nPsi Strike\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) Psychic damage."},
  ["creature.githzerai-psion.xmm2024"]={title="Githzerai Psion",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 137\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 169 (26d8 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 19 | WIS 18 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nPsionic Defense\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes three Psychic Warp attacks.\n\nPsychic Warp\n\nm,r 8, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h26 (4d10 + 4) Psychic damage, and the target has the githzerai's choice of (A) the XPHB condition until the start of the githzerai's next turn or (B) the XPHB condition, provided the target is a Large or smaller creature."},
  ["creature.githzerai-traveler.mpp2014"]={title="Githzerai Traveler",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 44 (8d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes three Unarmed Strike attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 4 (1d8) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nMatter Manipulation {@recharge 4}\n\nThe githzerai manipulates the energy of the plane of existence it's on to produce one of the following effects (choose one or roll a d6):\n\n• 1-2: Astral Step The githzerai can teleport, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 40 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. In addition, its walking speed increases to 40 feet until the start of its next turn.\n\n• 3-4: Growth Flowers and vines grow around the githzerai until the start of its next turn, then vanish; the ground within 15 feet of the githzerai is difficult terrain for other creatures while the flowers and vines are present.\n\n• 5-6: Retaliating Light Multicolored lights surround the githzerai until the start of its next turn. For the effect's duration, whenever a creature within 5 feet of the githzerai hits it with a melee attack roll, that creature takes 3 (1d6) force damage, as magic lashes out in retribution."},
  ["creature.githzerai-uniter.mpp2014"]={title="Githzerai Uniter",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 123 (19d8 + 38)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 17 | CON 15 | INT 15 | WIS 17 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes three Unarmed Strike or Psychic Bolt attacks. It can replace any of these attacks with one use of its Pacifying Touch.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage.\n\nPsychic Bolt\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h17 (5d6) psychic damage.\n\nPacifying Touch\n\nThe githzerai touches one creature it can see within 5 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 14 Intelligence saving throw, or the githzerai chooses an action for that target: Attack, Cast a Spell, or Dash. The affected target can't take that action for 1 minute. At the end of each of the target's turns, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a successful save. A target that succeeds on the saving throw becomes immune to this githzerai's Pacifying Touch for 24 hours."},
  ["creature.githzerai-zerth.mm2014"]={title="Githzerai Zerth",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 161\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 84 (13d8 + 26)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 16 | WIS 17 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Gith\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPsychic Defense\n\nWhile the githzerai is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes two unarmed strikes.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 13 (3d8) psychic damage. This is a magic weapon attack."},
  ["creature.githzerai-zerth.xmm2024"]={title="Githzerai Zerth",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 137\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 84 (13d8 + 26)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 16 | WIS 17 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Gith\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nPsi-Powered Leap (2/Day)\n\nPsionic Defense (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe githzerai makes two Psi Strike attacks.\n\nPsi Strike\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 13 (3d8) Psychic damage."},
  ["creature.glabbagool.oota2014"]={title="Glabbagool",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 10\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 60 ft."},
  ["creature.glabrezu.mm2014"]={title="Glabrezu",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 58\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 157 (15d10 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 21 | INT 19 | WIS 17 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe glabrezu has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe glabrezu makes four attacks: two with its pincers and two with its fists. Alternatively, it makes two attacks with its pincers and casts one spell.\n\nPincer\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 15). The glabrezu has two pincers, each of which can grapple only one target.\n\nFist\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.glabrezu.xmm2024"]={title="Glabrezu",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 138\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 189 (18d10 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 21 | INT 19 | WIS 17 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDemonic Restoration\n\nIf the glabrezu dies outside the Abyss, its body dissolves into ichor, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its XPHB somewhere in the Abyss.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe glabrezu has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe glabrezu makes two Pincer attacks and uses Pummel or Spellcasting.\n\nPincer\n\nm 9, reach 10 ft. h16 (2d10 + 5) Slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 15) from one of two pincers.\n\nPummel\n\ndex 17, one creature XPHB by the glabrezu. actSaveFail 15 (3d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.gladiator.mm2014"]={title="Gladiator",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 346\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nThe gladiator has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nBrute\n\nA melee weapon deals one extra die of its damage when the gladiator hits with it (included in the attack).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gladiator makes three melee attacks or two ranged attacks.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. and range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nShield Bash\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h9 (2d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe gladiator adds 3 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the gladiator must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.gladiator.xmm2024"]={title="Gladiator",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 139\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gladiator makes three Spear attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Shield Bash.\n\nSpear\n\nm,r 7, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nShield Bash\n\nstr 15, one creature within 5 feet that the gladiator can see. actSaveFail 9 (2d4 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nactTrigger The gladiator is hit by a melee attack roll while holding a weapon. actResponse The gladiator adds 3 to its AC against that attack, possibly causing it to miss."},
  ["item.glaive.phb2014"]={title="Glaive",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.glaive.veor2014"]={title="Glaive",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 187 (22d8 + 88)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 16 | CON 19 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHeatsink\n\nWhen Glaive takes cold damage, her Overdrive immediately recharges.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nGlaive has advantage on attack rolls if at least one ally is within 5 feet of the creature she's attacking and the ally doesn't have the incapacitated condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nGlaive makes two Spiked Glaive attacks and two Serrated Bolt attacks.\n\nSpiked Glaive\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (1d10 + 5) piercing or slashing damage, or 14 (1d10 + 9) piercing or slashing damage if Glaive is in overdrive.\n\nSerrated Bolt\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h13 (3d6 + 3) piercing damage. If Glaive has advantage on the attack roll, the serrated bolt lodges in the target, and the target's speed is reduced by 10 feet until the serrated bolt is removed. A target's speed can be reduced by only one serrated bolt at a time. A creature can use its action to remove a serrated bolt lodged in itself or another creature within its reach; when the bolt is removed from a creature, that creature takes 5 (2d4) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nOverdrive (Recharges after Finishing a Short or Long Rest)\n\nGlaive enters a state of overdrive that lasts for 1 minute or until she has the incapacitated condition. While in overdrive, Glaive gains the following benefits:\n\n• Glaive has advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\n\n• When Glaive makes a melee weapon attack, she gains a +4 bonus to the damage roll.\n\n• Glaive's speed increases to 50 feet.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSelf-Preservation\n\nIn response to being hit by a weapon attack, Glaive reduces the damage by 11 (2d10)."},
  ["item.glaive.xphb2024"]={title="Glaive",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.glamoured-studded-leather.dmg2014"]={title="Glamoured Studded Leather",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC. You can also use a bonus action to speak the armor's command word and cause the armor to assume the appearance of a normal set of clothing or some other kind of armor. You decide what it looks like, including color, style, and accessories, but the armor retains its normal bulk and weight. The illusory appearance lasts until you use this property again or remove the armor."},
  ["magicitem.glamoured-studded-leather.xdmg2024"]={title="Glamoured Studded Leather",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 264\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to XPHB. You can also take a XPHB to cause the armor to assume the appearance of a normal set of clothing or some other kind of armor. You decide what it looks like—including color, style, and accessories—but the armor retains its normal bulk and weight. The illusory appearance lasts until you use this property again or doff the armor."},
  ["item.glass-bottle.phb2014"]={title="Glass Bottle",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA bottle holds 1½ pints of liquid."},
  ["item.glass-bottle.xphb2024"]={title="Glass Bottle",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Glass Bottle holds up to 1½ pints."},
  ["creature.glass-pegasus.wbtw2014"]={title="Glass Pegasus",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 59 (7d10 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 90\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Elvish and Sylvan but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.glassblower-s-tools.phb2014"]={title="Glassblower's Tools",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSomeone who is proficient with glassblower's tools has not only the ability to shape glass, but also specialized knowledge of the methods used to produce glass objects.\n\nComponents\n\nThe tools include a blowpipe, a small marver, blocks, and tweezers. You need a source of heat to work glass.\n\nArcana, History\n\nYour knowledge of glassmaking techniques aids you when you examine glass objects, such as potion bottles or glass items found in a treasure hoard. For instance, you can study how a glass potion bottle has been changed by its contents to help determine a potion's effects. (A potion might leave behind a residue, deform the glass, or stain it.)\n\nInvestigation\n\nWhen you study an area, your knowledge can aid you if the clues include broken glass or glass objects.\n\nIdentify Weakness\n\nWith 1 minute of study, you can identify the weak points in a glass object. Any damage dealt to the object by striking a weak spot is doubled.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nIdentify source of glass | 10\n\nDetermine what a glass object once held | 20"},
  ["item.glassblower-s-tools.xphb2024"]={title="Glassblower's Tools",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 220\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Intelligence\n\n• Utilize: Discern what a glass object held in the past 24 hours (15)\n\n• Craft: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["creature.glasswork-golem.wbtw2014"]={title="Glasswork Golem",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 36 (8d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the golem is embedded in a window and motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the golem move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the golem is animate.\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe golem regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn. If the golem takes bludgeoning or thunder damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the golem's next turn. The golem is destroyed only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe golem doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes two Glass Sword attacks.\n\nGlass Sword\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDazzling Light {@recharge 5}\n\nMagical, colored light springs from the golem in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the cone must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw or be blinded for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.glasya.coa2014"]={title="Glasya",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 380 (40d8 + 200)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 28 | CON 20 | INT 21 | WIS 25 | CHA 28\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic, radiant\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharm Aura\n\nWhen a creature moves to be within 120 feet of Glasya, they must succeed on a 23 Wisdom saving throw or have the charmed condition, treating Glasya as an ally, until they leave the aura. A creature that succeeds the saving throw is immune to this effect for 1 hour. Whenever a charmed creature takes damage, they may repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on a success.\n\nDominating Presence\n\nGlasya deals an additional 13 (2d12) psychic damage when attacking a charmed creature, and her attacks don't break charms.\n\nFiendish Regeneration\n\nGlasya regains 20 hit points at the start of her turn. If she takes radiant damage this trait doesn't function at the start of her next turn. Glasya dies only if she starts her turn with 0 hit points and is unable to regenerate. If Glasya is killed, her body slowly regenerates, returning to life 9 (2d8) weeks later.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Glasya fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nGlasya has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nGlasya makes four attacks using Scourge of Shadow, Necrotic Grasp, or a combination of the two. She can replace one of the attacks with Mesmerizing Gaze.\n\nScourge of Shadow\n\nmw 20 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (3d4 + 12) slashing damage, plus 5 (2d4) necrotic damage. This attack scores a critical on a roll of 18, 19, or 20.\n\nNecrotic Grasp\n\nGlasya summons necrotic hands to grope and claw at a creature she can see within 90 feet of her. The target must make a 25 Constitution saving throw, taking 20 (2d10 + 9) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nMesmerizing Gaze\n\nGlasya focuses her gaze in a 60-foot cone in front of her. Each creature of her choice within the cone must make a 23 Charisma saving throw or have the charmed condition until the end of their next turn. While charmed, creatures automatically fail saving throws from abilities used by Glasya and move to be as close to her as possible.\n\nDeathly Exclamation (1/Day)\n\nGlasya targets a creature she can see within 60 feet of her. The target must make a 25 Constitution saving throw, taking 61 (7d8 + 30) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A Humanoid killed by this ability rises at the start of Glasya's next turn as a zombie permanently under her command.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nWhip\n\nGlasya makes a Scourge of Shadow attack.\n\nDisorient (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nGlasya casts Confusion (30-foot-radius, spell save 25), but only lasting until the end of Glasya's next turn.\n\nCall Underling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nGlasya summons an allied erinyes in an unoccupied space that she can see."},
  ["item.glaur.scag2014"]={title="Glaur",subtitle="Item - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\nRaridade: none\n\nShort, curved horns like a cornucopia. Played with valves, glaur sound like trumpets, while those without valves, known as gloon, have a more mournful sound."},
  ["spell.glibness.phb2014"]={title="Glibness",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\nUntil the spell ends, when you make a Charisma check, you can replace the number you roll with a 15. Additionally, no matter what you say, magic that would determine if you are telling the truth indicates that you are being truthful."},
  ["spell.glibness.xphb2024"]={title="Glibness",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 279\n\nUntil the spell ends, when you make a Charisma check, you can replace the number you roll with a 15. Additionally, no matter what you say, magic that would determine if you are telling the truth indicates that you are being truthful."},
  ["traphazard.glittermoss.nf2014"]={title="Glittermoss",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - NF - 2014",body="Intense fields of unstable magic can produce a sparkling, multicolored moss called glittermoss. A patch of glittermoss covers a 5-foot square. Glittermoss is often found near NF (see earlier in this chapter), though it doesn't grow in direct sunlight.\n\nA creature that comes into contact with glittermoss makes a 12 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 11 (2d10) Radiant damage and has the XPHB condition. While Blinded in this way, the creature is illuminated by glittering spores and sheds XPHB in a 10-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 10 feet. The creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nGlittermoss spores can leap to nearby creatures. While an affected creature is Blinded due to glittermoss, any creature that starts its turn within the Bright Light the affected creature sheds makes a 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 11 (2d10) Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nAny amount of Fire or Necrotic damage destroys a patch of glittermoss instantly."},
  ["creature.gloam.wbtw2014"]={title="Gloam",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 93\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 2 (1d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe cat has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 0 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1 slashing damage.\n\nCloud of Dust\n\nOn its first turn in combat or when it is reduced to 0 hit points, the cat expels a cloud of dust that acts as dust of sneezing and choking"},
  ["creature.gloamwing.ggr2014"]={title="Gloamwing",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 136 (16d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Link\n\nIf its specter rider is reduced to 0 hit points, the gloamwing is destroyed.\n\nFlyby\n\nThe gloamwing doesn't provoke an opportunity attack when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the gloamwing has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gloamwing makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (3d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["spell.globe-of-invulnerability.phb2014"]={title="Globe of Invulnerability",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\nAn immobile, faintly shimmering barrier springs into existence in a 10-foot radius around you and remains for the duration.\n\nAny spell of 5th level or lower cast from outside the barrier can't affect creatures or objects within it, even if the spell is cast using a higher level spell slot. Such a spell can target creatures and objects within the barrier, but the spell has no effect on them. Similarly, the area within the barrier is excluded from the areas affected by such spells."},
  ["spell.globe-of-invulnerability.xphb2024"]={title="Globe of Invulnerability",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 279\n\nAn immobile, shimmering barrier appears in a 10-foot XPHB around you and remains for the duration.\n\nAny spell of level 5 or lower cast from outside the barrier can't affect anything within it. Such a spell can target creatures and objects within the barrier, but the spell has no effect on them. Similarly, the area within the barrier is excluded from areas of effect created by such spells."},
  ["creature.gloine-nathair-nathair.llk2014"]={title="Gloine Nathair-Nathair",subtitle="Criatura - LLK - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead\n\nImunidades: poison, necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPetrifying Gaze\n\nWhen a creature that can see the medusa's eyes starts its turn within 30 feet of the medusa, the medusa can force it to make a 14 Constitution saving throw if the medusa isn't incapacitated and can see the creature. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the creature is instantly petrified. Otherwise, a creature that fails the save begins to turn to glass and is restrained. The restrained creature must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn, becoming petrified on a failure or ending the effect on a success. The petrification lasts until the creature is freed by the greater restoration spell or other magic.\n\nUnless surprised, a creature can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If the creature does so, it can't see the medusa until the start of its next turn, when it can avert its eyes again. If the creature looks at the medusa in the meantime, it must immediately make the save.\n\nIf the medusa sees itself reflected on a polished surface within 30 feet of it and in an area of bright light, the medusa is, due to its curse, affected by its own gaze."},
  ["subclass.gloom-stalker.xge2024.ranger.gloom-stalker.0"]={title="Gloom Stalker",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Dread Ambusher\n\nPagina: 41\n\nAt 3rd level, you master the art of the ambush. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Wisdom modifier.\n\nAt the start of your first turn of each combat, your walking speed increases by 10 feet, which lasts until the end of that turn. If you take the Attack action on that turn, you can make one additional weapon attack as part of that action. If that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's damage type.\n\nNivel 3 - Dread Ambusher\n\nPagina: 125\n\nYou have mastered the art of creating fearsome ambushes, granting you the following benefits.\n\nAmbusher's Leap\n\nAt the start of your first turn of each combat, your XPHB increases by 10 feet until the end of that turn.\n\nDreadful Strike\n\nWhen you attack a creature and hit it with a weapon, you can deal an extra 2d6 Psychic damage. You can use this benefit only once per turn, you can use it a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nInitiative Bonus\n\nWhen you roll XPHB, you can add your Wisdom modifier to the roll.\n\nNivel 3 - Dread Ambusher\n\nNivel 3 - Gloom Stalker\n\nPagina: 41\n\nGloom Stalkers are at home in the darkest places: deep under the earth, in gloomy alleyways, in primeval forests, and wherever else the light dims. Most folk enter such places with trepidation, but a Gloom Stalker ventures boldly into the darkness, seeking to ambush threats before they can reach the broader world. Such rangers are often found in the Underdark, but they will go any place where evil lurks in the shadows.\n\nNivel 3 - Gloom Stalker\n\nPagina: 125\n\nDraw on Shadow Magic to Fight Your Foes\n\nGloom Stalkers are at home in the darkest places, wielding magic drawn from the Shadowfell to combat enemies that lurk in darkness.\n\nNivel 3 - Gloom Stalker Magic\n\nPagina: 41\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Gloom Stalker Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.\n\nRanger Level | Spells\n\n3rd | disguise self\n\n5th | rope trick\n\n9th | fear\n\n13th | greater invisibility\n\n17th | seeming\n\nNivel 3 - Gloom Stalker Spells\n\nPagina: 126\n\nWhen you reach a Ranger level specified in the Gloom Stalker Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nRanger Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Umbral Sight\n\nPagina: 41\n\nAt 3rd level, you gain darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision from your race, its range increases by 30 feet.\n\nYou are also adept at evading creatures that rely on darkvision. While in darkness, you are invisible to any creature that relies on darkvision to see you in that darkness.\n\nNivel 3 - Umbral Sight\n\nPagina: 126\n\nYou gain XPHB with a range of 60 feet. If you already have XPHB when you gain this feature, its range increases by 60 feet.\n\nYou are also adept at evading creatures that rely on XPHB. While entirely in XPHB, you have the XPHB condition to any creature that relies on XPHB to see you in that XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Umbral Sight\n\nNivel 3 - Umbral Sight\n\nNivel 7 - Iron Mind\n\nPagina: 41\n\nBy 7th level, you have honed your ability to resist the mind-altering powers of your prey. You gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws. If you already have this proficiency, you instead gain proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma saving throws (your choice).\n\nNivel 7 - Iron Mind\n\nPagina: 126\n\nYou have honed your ability to resist mind-altering powers. You gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws. If you already have this proficiency, you instead gain proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma saving throws (your choice).\n\nNivel 7 - Iron Mind\n\nNivel 7 - Iron Mind\n\nNivel 11 - Stalker's Flurry\n\nPagina: 41\n\nAt 11th level, you learn to attack with such unexpected speed that you can turn a miss into another strike. Once on each of your turns when you miss with a weapon attack, you can make another weapon attack as part of the same action.\n\nNivel 11 - Stalker's Flurry\n\nPagina: 126\n\nThe Psychic damage of your Dreadful Strike becomes 2d8. In addition, when you use the Dreadful Strike effect of your Dread Ambusher feature, you can cause one of the following additional effects.\n\nSudden Strike\n\nYou can make another attack with the same weapon against a different creature that is within 5 feet of the original target and that is within the weapon's range.\n\nMass Fear\n\nThe target and each creature within 10 feet of it must make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature has the XPHB condition until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 11 - Stalker's Flurry\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge\n\nPagina: 41\n\nStarting at 15th level, you can dodge in unforeseen ways, with wisps of supernatural shadow around you. Whenever a creature makes an attack roll against you and doesn't have advantage on the roll, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on it. You must use this feature before you know the outcome of the attack roll.\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge\n\nPagina: 126\n\nWhen a creature makes an attack roll against you, you can take a XPHB to impose XPHB on that roll. Whether the attack hits or misses, you can then teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge"},
  ["feature.gloom-stalker.xge2024.ranger.gloom-stalker.3"]={title="Gloom Stalker",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 41\n\nGloom Stalkers are at home in the darkest places: deep under the earth, in gloomy alleyways, in primeval forests, and wherever else the light dims. Most folk enter such places with trepidation, but a Gloom Stalker ventures boldly into the darkness, seeking to ambush threats before they can reach the broader world. Such rangers are often found in the Underdark, but they will go any place where evil lurks in the shadows."},
