ain proficiency in Intelligence or Charisma saving throws (your choice).\n\nNivel 7 - Iron Mind\n\nNivel 7 - Iron Mind\n\nNivel 11 - Stalker's Flurry\n\nPagina: 41\n\nAt 11th level, you learn to attack with such unexpected speed that you can turn a miss into another strike. Once on each of your turns when you miss with a weapon attack, you can make another weapon attack as part of the same action.\n\nNivel 11 - Stalker's Flurry\n\nPagina: 126\n\nThe Psychic damage of your Dreadful Strike becomes 2d8. In addition, when you use the Dreadful Strike effect of your Dread Ambusher feature, you can cause one of the following additional effects.\n\nSudden Strike\n\nYou can make another attack with the same weapon against a different creature that is within 5 feet of the original target and that is within the weapon's range.\n\nMass Fear\n\nThe target and each creature within 10 feet of it must make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature has the XPHB condition until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 11 - Stalker's Flurry\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge\n\nPagina: 41\n\nStarting at 15th level, you can dodge in unforeseen ways, with wisps of supernatural shadow around you. Whenever a creature makes an attack roll against you and doesn't have advantage on the roll, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on it. You must use this feature before you know the outcome of the attack roll.\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge\n\nPagina: 126\n\nWhen a creature makes an attack roll against you, you can take a XPHB to impose XPHB on that roll. Whether the attack hits or misses, you can then teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge"},
  ["feature.gloom-stalker.xphb2024.ranger.gloom-stalker.3"]={title="Gloom Stalker",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 125\n\nDraw on Shadow Magic to Fight Your Foes\n\nGloom Stalkers are at home in the darkest places, wielding magic drawn from the Shadowfell to combat enemies that lurk in darkness."},
  ["feature.gloom-stalker-magic.xge2024.ranger.gloom-stalker.3"]={title="Gloom Stalker Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 41\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you learn an additional spell when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Gloom Stalker Spells table. The spell counts as a ranger spell for you, but it doesn't count against the number of ranger spells you know.\n\nRanger Level | Spells\n\n3rd | disguise self\n\n5th | rope trick\n\n9th | fear\n\n13th | greater invisibility\n\n17th | seeming"},
  ["feature.gloom-stalker-spells.xphb2024.ranger.gloom-stalker.3"]={title="Gloom Stalker Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 126\n\nWhen you reach a Ranger level specified in the Gloom Stalker Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nRanger Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB"},
  ["creature.gloom-weaver.mtf2014"]={title="Gloom Weaver",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 14/17\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 15 | WIS 12 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBurden of Time\n\nBeasts and humanoids, other than shadar-kai, have disadvantage on saving throws while within 10 feet of the gloom weaver.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe gloom weaver has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put it to sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gloom weaver makes two spear attacks and casts one spell that takes 1 action to cast.\n\nShadow Spear\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 26 (4d12) necrotic damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 26 (4d12) necrotic damage if used with two hands.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nMisty Escape (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nWhen the gloom weaver takes damage, it turns invisible and teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. It remains invisible until the start of its next turn or until it attacks or casts a spell."},
  ["creature.gloomstalker.egw2014"]={title="Gloomstalker",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 291\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 5 | WIS 17 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nVulnerabilidades: radiant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShadowstep\n\nAs a bonus action, the gloomstalker can teleport up to 40 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the gloomstalker has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gloomstalker makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h15 (2d8 + 6) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage.\n\nSnatch\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage, and the target is grappled (escape 17). While grappled in this way, the target is restrained.\n\nShriek {@recharge}\n\nThe gloomstalker emits a terrible shriek. Each enemy within 60 feet of the gloomstalker that can hear it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed until the end of the enemy's next turn."},
  ["feature.glorious-defense.tce2014.paladin.glory.15"]={title="Glorious Defense",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.glorious-defense.xphb2024.paladin.glory.15"]={title="Glorious Defense",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.gloves-of-missile-snaring.dmg2014"]={title="Gloves of Missile Snaring",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThese gloves seem to almost meld into your hands when you don them. When a ranged weapon attack hits you while you're wearing them, you can use your reaction to reduce the damage by 1d10 + your Dexterity modifier, provided that you have a free hand. If you reduce the damage to 0, you can catch the missile if it is small enough for you to hold in that hand."},
  ["magicitem.gloves-of-missile-snaring.xdmg2024"]={title="Gloves of Missile Snaring",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nIf you're hit by an attack roll made with a Ranged or Thrown weapon while wearing these gloves, you can take a XPHB to reduce the damage by 1d10 plus your Dexterity modifier if you have a free hand. If you reduce the damage to 0, you can catch the ammunition or weapon if it is small enough for you to hold in that hand."},
  ["magicitem.gloves-of-soul-catching.cm2014"]={title="Gloves of Soul Catching",subtitle="Item Magico - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nYour Constitution score is 20 while you wear these gloves. This property of the gloves has no effect on you if your Constitution is already 20 or higher.\n\nAfter making a successful unarmed strike while wearing these gloves, you can use the gloves to deal an extra 2d10 force damage to the target, and you regain a number of hit points equal to the force damage dealt. Alternatively, instead of regaining hit points in this way, you can choose to gain advantage on one attack roll, ability check, or saving throw you make before the end of your next turn."},
  ["magicitem.gloves-of-swimming-and-climbing.dmg2014"]={title="Gloves of Swimming and Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing these gloves, climbing and swimming don't cost you extra movement, and you gain a +5 bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks made to climb or swim."},
  ["magicitem.gloves-of-swimming-and-climbing.xdmg2024"]={title="Gloves of Swimming and Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing these gloves, climbing and swimming don't cost you extra movement, and you gain a +5 bonus to Strength (XPHB) checks made to climb or swim."},
  ["magicitem.gloves-of-thievery.dmg2014"]={title="Gloves of Thievery",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThese gloves are invisible while worn. While wearing them, you gain a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks and Dexterity checks made to pick locks."},
  ["magicitem.gloves-of-thievery.xdmg2024"]={title="Gloves of Thievery",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThese gloves are imperceptible while worn. While wearing them, you gain a +5 bonus to Dexterity (XPHB) checks.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["magicitem.glowrune-pigment.bgg2014"]={title="Glowrune Pigment",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis set of 1d4 + 2 small paint pots contains pigments mixed from crushed luminescent gemstones. This magical paint bestows temporary magical gifts on creatures with runes drawn on their skin with this paint.\n\nOne paint pot contains enough pigment to paint one rune. A creature can spend 10 minutes to paint one of the following runes onto itself or another creature:\n\nJourney Rune\n\ndifficult terrain doesn't cost the painted creature extra movement.\n\nLife Rune\n\nThe painted creature gains 10 temporary hit points and has advantage on death saving throws.\n\nLight Rune\n\nThe painted creature gains darkvision to a range of 30 feet. If the painted creature already has darkvision from another source, the range of its darkvision increases by 30 feet.\n\nMountain Rune\n\nThe painted creature is immune to being knocked prone and has advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws.\n\nShield Rune\n\nThe painted creature has advantage on Dexterity saving throws against effects that deal damage.\n\nA creature can benefit from only one painted rune at a time, so a new rune painted on a creature has no effect unless the old one is removed first. The rune's benefits last for 8 hours or until the painted creature uses its action to wipe away the rune."},
  ["spell.glyph-of-warding.phb2014"]={title="Glyph of Warding",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\nWhen you cast this spell, you inscribe a glyph that later unleashes a magical effect. You inscribe it either on a surface (such as a table or a section of floor or wall) or within an object that can be closed (such as a book, a scroll, or a treasure chest) to conceal the glyph. The glyph can cover an area no larger than 10 feet in diameter. If the surface or object is moved more than 10 feet from where you cast this spell, the glyph is broken, and the spell ends without being triggered.\n\nThe glyph is nearly invisible and requires a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC to be found.\n\nYou decide what triggers the glyph when you cast the spell. For glyphs inscribed on a surface, the most typical triggers include touching or standing on the glyph, removing another object covering the glyph, approaching within a certain distance of the glyph, or manipulating the object on which the glyph is inscribed. For glyphs inscribed within an object, the most common triggers include opening that object, approaching within a certain distance of the object, or seeing or reading the glyph. Once a glyph is triggered, this spell ends.\n\nYou can further refine the trigger so the spell activates only under certain circumstances or according to physical characteristics (such as height or weight), creature kind (for example, the ward could be set to affect aberrations or drow), or alignment. You can also set conditions for creatures that don't trigger the glyph, such as those who say a certain password.\n\nWhen you inscribe the glyph, choose explosive runes or a spell glyph.\n\nExplosive Runes\n\nWhen triggered, the glyph erupts with magical energy in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on the glyph. The sphere spreads around corners. Each creature in the area must make a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 5d8 acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage on a failed saving throw (your choice when you create the glyph), or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nSpell Glyph\n\nYou can store a prepared spell of 3rd level or lower in the glyph by casting it as part of creating the glyph. The spell must target a single creature or an area. The spell being stored has no immediate effect when cast in this way. When the glyph is triggered, the stored spell is cast. If the spell has a target, it targets the creature that triggered the glyph. If the spell affects an area, the area is centered on that creature. If the spell summons hostile creatures or creates harmful objects or traps, they appear as close as possible to the intruder and attack it. If the spell requires concentration, it lasts until the end of its full duration."},
  ["spell.glyph-of-warding.xphb2024"]={title="Glyph of Warding",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 279\n\nYou inscribe a glyph that later unleashes a magical effect. You inscribe it either on a surface (such as a table or a section of floor) or within an object that can be closed (such as a book or chest) to conceal the glyph. The glyph can cover an area no larger than 10 feet in diameter. If the surface or object is moved more than 10 feet from where you cast this spell, the glyph is broken, and the spell ends without being triggered.\n\nThe glyph is nearly imperceptible and requires a successful Wisdom (XPHB) check against your spell save DC to notice.\n\nWhen you inscribe the glyph, you set its trigger and choose whether it's an explosive rune or a spell glyph, as explained below.\n\nSet the Trigger\n\nYou decide what triggers the glyph when you cast the spell. For glyphs inscribed on a surface, common triggers include touching or stepping on the glyph, removing another object covering it, or approaching within a certain distance of it. For glyphs inscribed within an object, common triggers include opening that object or seeing the glyph. Once a glyph is triggered, this spell ends.\n\nYou can refine the trigger so that only creatures of certain types activate it (for example, the glyph could be set to affect Aberrations). You can also set conditions for creatures that don't trigger the glyph, such as those who say a certain password.\n\nExplosive Rune\n\nWhen triggered, the glyph erupts with magical energy in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on the glyph. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 5d8 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (your choice when you create the glyph) on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nSpell Glyph\n\nYou can store a prepared spell of level 3 or lower in the glyph by casting it as part of creating the glyph. The spell must target a single creature or an area. The spell being stored has no immediate effect when cast in this way.\n\nWhen the glyph is triggered, the stored spell takes effect. If the spell has a target, it targets the creature that triggered the glyph. If the spell affects an area, the area is centered on that creature. If the spell summons XPHB creatures or creates harmful objects or traps, they appear as close as possible to the intruder and attack it. If the spell requires XPHB, it lasts until the end of its full duration."},
  ["creature.glyphic-shroomlight.oota2014"]={title="Glyphic Shroomlight",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 103\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.glyster.wdmm2014"]={title="Glyster",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 241\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.gnarlid.psz2014"]={title="Gnarlid",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["species.gnoll.dmg2014"]={title="Gnoll",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nBite\n\nYour fanged maw is a natural weapon, which you can use to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with it, you deal piercing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nRampage\n\nWhen you reduce a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on your turn, you can take a bonus action to move up to half your speed and make a bite attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll.mm2014"]={title="Gnoll",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 22 (5d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 11 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["language.gnoll.mm2014"]={title="Gnoll",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 163"},
  ["language.gnoll.xmm2024"]={title="Gnoll",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 141"},
  ["creature.gnoll-demoniac.xmm2024"]={title="Gnoll Demoniac",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 141\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 135 (18d8 + 54)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 14 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Gnoll\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes two Abyssal Strike attacks.\n\nAbyssal Strike\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h20 (5d6 + 3) Poison damage.\n\nHunger of Yeenoghu {@recharge 5}\n\nThe gnoll conjures a 30-foot XPHB of magical XPHB originating from a point it can see within 60 feet, which lasts for 1 minute or until the gnoll's XPHB ends on it. This area is XPHB. dex 14, any creature that starts its turn in this area or enters it for the first time on a turn. actSaveFail 28 (8d6) Necrotic damage, and the gnoll or a creature of its choice it can see gains 10 XPHB. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage (2/Day)\n\nImmediately after dealing damage to a creature that is already XPHB, the gnoll moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Abyssal Strike attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll-fang-of-yeenoghu.mm2014"]={title="Gnoll Fang of Yeenoghu",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 15 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Gnoll\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or take 7 (2d6) poison damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.gnoll-fang-of-yeenoghu.xmm2024"]={title="Gnoll Fang of Yeenoghu",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 141\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 71 (11d8 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 15 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Gnoll\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes one Bite attack and two Bone Flail attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the gnoll's next turn.\n\nBone Flail\n\nm 5, reach 10 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage (2/Day)\n\nImmediately after dealing damage to a creature that is already XPHB, the gnoll moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Bite attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll-flesh-gnawer.mpmm2014"]={title="Gnoll Flesh Gnawer",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes one Bite attack and two Shortsword attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSudden Rush\n\nUntil the end of the turn, the gnoll's speed increases by 60 feet and it doesn't provoke opportunity attack.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage\n\nAfter the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll moves up to half its speed and makes a Bite attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll-flesh-gnawer.vgm2014"]={title="Gnoll Flesh Gnawer",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its shortsword.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSudden Rush\n\nUntil the end of the turn, the gnoll's speed increases by 60 feet and it doesn't provoke opportunity attacks."},
  ["creature.gnoll-hunter.mpmm2014"]={title="Gnoll Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes two Bite, Spear, or Longbow attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage when used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage, and the target's speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage\n\nAfter the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll moves up to half its speed and makes a Bite attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll-hunter.vgm2014"]={title="Gnoll Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes two melee attacks with its spear or two ranged attacks with its longbow.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage when used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage, and the target's speed is reduced by 10 feet until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.gnoll-pack-lord.mm2014"]={title="Gnoll Pack Lord",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen the gnoll reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes two attacks, either with its glaive or its longbow, and uses its Incite Rampage if it can.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nGlaive\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nIncite Rampage {@recharge 5}\n\nOne creature the gnoll can see within 30 feet of it can use its reaction to make a melee attack if it can hear the gnoll and has the Rampage trait."},
  ["creature.gnoll-pack-lord.xmm2024"]={title="Gnoll Pack Lord",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 140\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gnoll makes two attacks, using Bone Whip or Bone Javelin in any combination, and it uses Incite Rampage if available.\n\nBone Whip\n\nm 5, reach 10 ft. h8 (2d4 + 3) Slashing damage.\n\nBone Javelin\n\nr 5, range 30/120 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\nIncite Rampage {@recharge 5}\n\nThe gnoll targets another creature it can see within 60 feet of itself that has the Rampage XPHB. The target can take a XPHB to make one melee attack.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage (2/Day)\n\nImmediately after dealing damage to a creature that is already XPHB, the gnoll moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Bone Whip attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll-vampire.idrotf2014"]={title="Gnoll Vampire",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 290\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 93 (11d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 18 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Gnoll\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe vampire has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nRampage\n\nWhen it reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the vampire can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vampire regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point and isn't in sunlight or running water. If the vampire takes radiant damage or damage from PHB, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vampire's next turn.\n\nShapechanger\n\nIf the vampire isn't in sunlight, it can use its action to polymorph into a Large hyena or a Medium cloud of mist, or back into its true form.\n\nWhile in hyena form, the vampire can't speak, and its walking speed is 50 feet. Its statistics, other than its size and speed, are unchanged. Anything it is wearing transforms with it, but nothing it is carrying does. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nWhile in mist form, the vampire can't take any actions, speak, or manipulate objects. it is weightless, has a flying speed of 20 feet, can hover, and can enter a hostile creature's space and stop there. In addition, if air can pass through a space, the mist can do so without squeezing, and it can't pass through water. It has advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws, and it is immune to all nonmagical damage, except the damage it takes from sunlight.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe vampire doesn't require air.\n\nVampire Weaknesses\n\nThe vampire has the following flaws:\n\n• Enraged by Celestial\n\n• Repulsed by Perfume\n\n• Stake to the Heart\n\n• Sunlight Hypersensitivity\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Vampire Form Only)\n\nThe vampire makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite (Hyena or Vampire Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) necrotic damage. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the necrotic damage taken, and the vampire regains hit points equal to that amount. The reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. the target dies if its hit point maximum is reduced to 0.\n\nClaws (Vampire Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d4 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nFrightful Cackle (Hyena or Vampire Form Only)\n\nThe vampire emits a bone-chilling cackle. Each creature of the vampire's choice that is within 120 feet of the vampire and can hear its cackle must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the vampire's Frightful Cackle for the next 24 hours.\n\nSickening Gaze (Hyena or Vampire Form Only)\n\nThe vampire targets one humanoid it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see the vampire, the target must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw against this magic or be poisoned for 24 hours. A creature whose saving throw is successful is immune to this vampire's Sickening Gaze for 24 hours."},
  ["creature.gnoll-warrior.wtthc2014"]={title="Gnoll Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.gnoll-warrior.xmm2024"]={title="Gnoll Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 140\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 11 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Gnoll\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRend\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\nBone Bow\n\nr 3, range 150/600 ft. h6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage (1/Day)\n\nImmediately after dealing damage to a creature that is already XPHB, the gnoll moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll-witherling.mpmm2014"]={title="Gnoll Witherling",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 8 | CON 12 | INT 5 | WIS 5 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Gnoll but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe witherling doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe witherling makes two Bite or Spiked Club attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) necrotic damage.\n\nSpiked Club\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRampage\n\nAfter the witherling reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, the gnoll moves up to half its speed and makes one Bite attack.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nVengeful Strike\n\nIn response to a gnoll being reduced to 0 hit points within 30 feet of the witherling, the witherling makes one Bite or Spiked Club attack."},
  ["creature.gnoll-witherling.vgm2014"]={title="Gnoll Witherling",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 8 | CON 12 | INT 5 | WIS 5 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Gnoll but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRampage\n\nWhen the witherling reduces a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, it can take a bonus action to move up to half its speed and make a bite attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe witherling makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its club, or two with its club.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClub\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nVengeful Strike\n\nIn response to a gnoll being reduced to 0 hit points within 30 feet of the witherling, the witherling makes a melee attack."},
  ["species.gnome.phb2014"]={title="Gnome",subtitle="Especie - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\nAge\n\nGnomes mature at the same rate humans do, and most are expected to settle down into an adult life by around age 40. They can live 350 to almost 500 years.\n\nSize\n\nGnomes are between 3 and 4 feet tall and average about 40 pounds. Your size is Small.\n\nDarkvision\n\nAccustomed to life underground, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nGnome Cunning\n\nYou have advantage on all Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws against magic.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Gnomish. The Gnomish language, which uses the Dwarvish script, is renowned for its technical treatises and its catalogs of knowledge about the natural world."},
  ["species.gnome.xphb2024"]={title="Gnome",subtitle="Especie - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 191\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet.\n\nGnomish Cunning\n\nYou have XPHB on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws.\n\nGnomish Lineage\n\nYou are part of a lineage that grants you supernatural abilities. Choose one of the following options; whichever one you choose, Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for the spells you cast with this trait (choose the ability when you select the lineage):\n\n• Forest Gnome You know the XPHB cantrip. You also always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it without a spell slot a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB. You can also use any spell slots you have to cast the spell.\n\n• Rock Gnome You know the XPHB and XPHB cantrips. In addition, you can spend 10 minutes casting XPHB to create a Tiny clockwork device (AC 5, 1 HP), such as a toy, fire starter, or music box. When you create the device, you determine its function by choosing one effect from XPHB; the device produces that effect whenever you or another creature takes a XPHB to activate it with a touch. If the chosen effect has options within it, you choose one of those options for the device when you create it. For example, if you choose the spell's ignite-extinguish effect, you determine whether the device ignites or extinguishes fire; the device doesn't do both. You can have three such devices in existence at a time, and each falls apart 8 hours after its creation or when you dismantle it with a touch as a XPHB action."},
  ["species.gnome-deep.dmg2014"]={title="Gnome (Deep)",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nYou have an innate ability to cast the following spells, requiring no material components:\n\n• At will:\n\n• 1/day each:\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for these spells.\n\nStone Camouflage\n\nYou have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to hide in rocky terrain.\n\nGnome Cunning\n\nYou have advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws against magic.\n\nSuperior Darkvision\n\nAccustomed to life underground, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 120 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Gnomish, Terran, and Undercommon."},
  ["creature.gnome-ceremorph.idrotf2014"]={title="Gnome Ceremorph",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 303\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / S\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 58 (13d6 + 13)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 19 | WIS 17 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Gnomish, telepathy 120 ft., Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe ceremorph has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTentacles\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h15 (2d10 + 4) psychic damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 9) and must succeed on a 15 Intelligence saving throw or be stunned until this grapple ends.\n\nExtract Brain\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one incapacitated humanoid grappled by the ceremorph. h55 (10d10) piercing damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the ceremorph kills the target by extracting and devouring its brain.\n\nLaser Pistol\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 40/120 ft., one target. h12 (3d6 + 2) radiant damage.\n\nMind Blast {@recharge 5}\n\nThe ceremorph magically emits psychic energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 15 Intelligence saving throw or take 22 (4d8 + 4) psychic damage and be stunned for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.gnome-squidling.idrotf2014"]={title="Gnome Squidling",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 303\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 8\n\nPV: 10 (3d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15\n\nSTR 4 | DEX 7 | CON 10 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Deep Speech and Gnomish but can't speak, telepathy 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe squidling has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTentacles\n\nmw 0 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (2d4) psychic damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 7) and must succeed on a 7 Intelligence saving throw or be stunned until this grapple ends.\n\nExtract Brain\n\nmw 0 to hit, reach 5 ft., one incapacitated creature grappled by the squidling. h27 (5d10) piercing damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the squidling kills the target by extracting and devouring its brain.\n\nMind Tickle {@recharge 5}\n\nThe squidling magically emits psychic energy in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 7 Intelligence saving throw or take 2 (1d4) psychic damage and be stunned until the end of its next turn."},
  ["object.gnomeflinger.dsotdq2014"]={title="Gnomeflinger",subtitle="Objeto - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\nThe gnomeflinger is a catapult designed to hurl creatures, instead of projectiles, in a high arc. The gnomeflinger was designed in conjunction with the DSotDQ (see the DSotDQ section) to hasten transportation. The device can hold one Medium or smaller creature. Before it can be used, the gnomeflinger must be loaded and aimed. It takes 1 action to load the gnomeflinger, 1 action to aim it, and 1 action to fire it.\n\nWhile taking an action to aim the gnomeflinger, you set the maximum horizontal distance of the Fling Personnel action to 60 feet, 150 feet, or 300 feet."},
  ["magicitem.gnomengarde-grenade.dc2014"]={title="Gnomengarde Grenade",subtitle="Item Magico - DC - 2014",body="Raridade: varies\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis small metallic object is comprised of rune-covered parts made from different metals, linked together with a variety of gears, bands, bits, and bobs. The metals are all different colors, making the grenade shine with a rainbow of color when held up in the light.\n\nAs a bonus action, a creature can turn a special key to arm the grenade. Once armed, the grenade explodes in a matter of seconds. As an action, the wielder can hurl the grenade up to 120 feet. At the end of their turn, the grenade explodes. All creatures within 60 feet of the grenade when it explodes suffer the following effects:\n\n• Each creature must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much fire damage on a successful one.\n\n• Each creature must make a 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 28 (8d6) thunder damage and is stunned until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much thunder damage and is not stunned.\n\n• The wielder rolls on the chart* for the dmg three times, rerolling any duplicate results. Any effects that specify a target affect all creatures in range of the grenade when it explodes. Any effects that would affect the wielder of the wand instead affect the closest creature to the grenade when it goes off.\n\nThe grenade explodes immediately if a creature places it in an extradimensional space or teleports while in possession of it. The effects of the explosion will be felt at both the origin and terminus of the teleportation, but only affecting all creatures within 30 feet of either location."},
  ["language.gnomish.dsotdq2014"]={title="Gnomish",subtitle="Idioma - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.gnomish.erlw2014"]={title="Gnomish",subtitle="Idioma - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 6"},
  ["language.gnomish.phb2014"]={title="Gnomish",subtitle="Idioma - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 123\n\nThe Gnomish language, which uses the Dwarvish script, is renowned for its technical treatises and its catalogs of knowledge about the natural world."},
  ["language.gnomish.xphb2024"]={title="Gnomish",subtitle="Idioma - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 37"},
  ["optionalfeature.goading-attack.phb2014"]={title="Goading Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\nWhen you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend one superiority die to attempt to goad the target into attacking you. You add the superiority die to the attack's damage roll, and the target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target has disadvantage on all attack rolls against targets other than you until the end of your next turn."},
  ["optionalfeature.goading-attack.xphb2024"]={title="Goading Attack",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 95\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll, you can expend one Superiority Die to attempt to goad the target into attacking you. Add the Superiority Die to the attack's damage roll. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have XPHB on attack rolls against targets other than you until the end of your next turn."},
  ["creature.goat.mm2014"]={title="Goat",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 330\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 4 (1d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 10 | CON 11 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the goat moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a ram attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 2 (1d4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 10 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nSure-Footed\n\nThe goat has advantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws made against effects that would knock it prone.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.goat.phb2014"]={title="Goat",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.goat.xdmg2024"]={title="Goat",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.goat.xmm2024"]={title="Goat",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 362\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 4 (1d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 10 | CON 11 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nm 2, reach 5 ft. h1 Bludgeoning damage, or 2 (1d4) Bludgeoning damage if the goat moved 20+ feet straight toward the target immediately before the hit."},
  ["species.goblin.dmg2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nNimble Escape\n\nYou can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of your turns.\n\nDarkvision\n\nAccustomed to life underground, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Goblin."},
  ["language.goblin.dsotdq2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Idioma - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.goblin.erlw2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Idioma - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 6"},
  ["species.goblin.erlw2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Especie - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 26"},
  ["language.goblin.ggr2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nIn Ravnica, Goblin is a simplistic language with a limited vocabulary and fluid rules of grammar, unsuited for any sophisticated conversation."},
  ["species.goblin.ggr2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Especie - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 16"},
  ["creature.goblin.mm2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 166\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["species.goblin.mpmm2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are a Humanoid. You are also considered a goblinoid for any prerequisite or effect that requires you to be a goblinoid.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light and in darkness as if it were in dim light. You discern colors in that darkness only as shades of gray.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the charmed condition on yourself.\n\nFury of the Small\n\nWhen you damage a creature with an attack or a spell and the creature's size is larger than yours, you can cause the attack or spell to deal extra damage to the creature. The extra damage equals your proficiency bonus.\n\nYou can use this trait a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, regaining all expended uses when you finish a long rest, and you can use it no more than once per turn.\n\nNimble Escape\n\nYou can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of your turns."},
  ["language.goblin.phb2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Idioma - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 123"},
  ["species.goblin.psz2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Especie - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nAge\n\nGoblins mature faster than humans, reaching adulthood at around age 12. They also age noticeably faster than humans, and even the most cautious goblins rarely live longer than 50 years.\n\nAlignment\n\nMost goblins are wildly chaotic, though they have no particular inclination toward good or evil.\n\nSize\n\nGoblins average about 3 feet tall and weigh about 40 pounds. Your size is Small.\n\nDarkvision\n\nThanks to your heritage, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Goblin.\n\nGrit\n\nYou have resistance to fire damage and psychic damage. In addition, when you are wearing no armor, your AC is equal to 11 + your Dexterity modifier."},
  ["species.goblin.vgm2014"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Especie - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nAge\n\nGoblins reach adulthood at age 8 and live up to 60 years.\n\nSize\n\nGoblins are between 3 and 4 feet tall and weigh between 40 and 80 pounds. Your size is Small.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nFury of the Small\n\nWhen you damage a creature with an attack or a spell and the creature's size is larger than yours, you can cause the attack or spell to deal extra damage to the creature. The extra damage equals your level. Once you use this trait, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nNimble Escape\n\nYou can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of your turns.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Goblin."},
  ["language.goblin.xphb2024"]={title="Goblin",subtitle="Idioma - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 37"},
  ["species.goblin-dankwood.awm2014"]={title="Goblin (Dankwood)",subtitle="Especie - AWM - 2014",body="Pagina: 35"},
  ["creature.goblin-boss.mm2014"]={title="Goblin Boss",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 166\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 21 (6d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe goblin makes two attacks with its scimitar. The second attack has disadvantage.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nRedirect Attack\n\nWhen a creature the goblin can see targets it with an attack, the goblin chooses another goblin within 5 feet of it. The two goblins swap places, and the chosen goblin becomes the target instead."},
  ["creature.goblin-boss.xmm2024"]={title="Goblin Boss",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 143\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 21 (6d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe goblin makes two attacks, using Scimitar or Shortbow in any combination.\n\nScimitar\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, plus 2 (1d4) Slashing damage if the attack roll had XPHB.\n\nShortbow\n\nr 4, range 80/320 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, plus 2 (1d4) Piercing damage if the attack roll had XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin takes the XPHB or XPHB action.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nRedirect Attack\n\nactTrigger A creature the goblin can see makes an attack roll against it. actResponse The goblin chooses a Small or Medium ally within 5 feet of itself. The goblin and that ally swap places, and the ally becomes the target of the attack instead."},
  ["creature.goblin-boss-archer.pabtso2014"]={title="Goblin Boss Archer",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.goblin-commoner.tftyp2014"]={title="Goblin Commoner",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 3 (1d6)\n\nSTR 8\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClub\n\nmw 1 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1 (1d4 - 1) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.goblin-gang-member.kkw2014"]={title="Goblin Gang Member",subtitle="Criatura - KKW - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 10 (3d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 16 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nLight Crossbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.goblin-hexer.xmm2024"]={title="Goblin Hexer",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 143\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 45 (10d6 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe goblin makes two Hex Stick attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nHex Stick\n\nm,r 5, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Psychic damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nJinx\n\nactTrigger A creature the goblin can see hits it with an attack roll. dwis 13, the triggering creature. actSaveFail The attack misses instead."},
  ["creature.goblin-minion.xmm2024"]={title="Goblin Minion",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nm,r 4, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin takes the XPHB or XPHB action."},
  ["creature.goblin-psi-brawler.pabtso2014"]={title="Goblin Psi Brawler",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / S\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 31 (7d6 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 17 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin, telepathy 30 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMental Burst\n\nWhen the goblin dies, its pent-up mental energy explodes in a psychic blast. Each creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 13 Intelligence saving throw or take 5 (2d4) psychic damage.\n\nMental Fortitude\n\nThe goblin has advantage on saving throws against effects that would make it have the charmed or frightened condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe goblin makes two Unarmed Strike attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin takes the Disengage or Hide action.\n\nTelekinetic Shove\n\nThe goblin targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of itself with a thrust of telekinetic force. The target must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition."},
  ["creature.goblin-psi-commander.pabtso2014"]={title="Goblin Psi Commander",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / S\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 58 (13d6 + 13)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 19 | CON 13 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMental Burst\n\nWhen the goblin dies, its pent-up mental energy explodes in a psychic blast. Each creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 13 Intelligence saving throw or take 10 (4d4) psychic damage.\n\nMental Fortitude\n\nThe goblin has advantage on saving throws against effects that would make it have the charmed or frightened conditions.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe goblin makes three Psychic Blade attacks.\n\nPsychic Blade\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one creature. h11 (2d6 + 4) psychic damage, and the target must subtract 1d4 from the next attack roll or saving throw it makes before the end of the goblin's next turn.\n\nSynaptic Rend {@recharge 5}\n\nThe goblin unleashes a 30-foot-radius sphere of psychic energy, centered on a point the goblin can see within 60 feet of itself. Each creature in that area must make a 13 Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 14 (4d6) psychic damage and has the incapacitated condition until the end of the goblin's next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin takes the Disengage or Hide action.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nPsionic Shield\n\nWhen the goblin or one of its allies within 15 feet of it is hit by an attack roll, the goblin conjures a shield of force. The target of the attack gains a +3 bonus to its AC against the triggering attack roll, potentially causing it to miss."},
  ["creature.goblin-warrior.wtthc2014"]={title="Goblin Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.goblin-warrior.xmm2024"]={title="Goblin Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 10 (3d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 8 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nScimitar\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage, plus 2 (1d4) Slashing damage if the attack roll had XPHB.\n\nShortbow\n\nr 4, range 80/320 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage, plus 2 (1d4) Piercing damage if the attack roll had XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin takes the XPHB or XPHB action."},
  ["magicitem.goggles-of-night.dmg2014"]={title="Goggles of Night",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing these dark lenses, you have darkvision out to a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, wearing the goggles increases its range by 60 feet."},
  ["magicitem.goggles-of-night.xdmg2024"]={title="Goggles of Night",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing these dark lenses, you have XPHB out to 60 feet. If you already have XPHB, wearing the goggles increases its range by 60 feet.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["magicitem.goggles-of-object-reading.egw2014"]={title="Goggles of Object Reading",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThese leather-framed goggles feature purple crystal lenses. While wearing the goggles, you have advantage on Intelligence (Arcana) checks made to reveal information about a creature or object you can see.\n\nIn addition, you can cast the identify spell using the googles. Once you do so, you can't do so again until the next dawn."},
  ["deity.goibhniu.phb2014"]={title="Goibhniu",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["item.gold.phb2014"]={title="Gold",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.gold.xdmg2024"]={title="Gold",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.gold-gp.phb2014"]={title="Gold (gp)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 143\n\nRaridade: none\n\nCommon coins come in several different denominations based on the relative worth of the metal from which they are made. The three most common coins are the gold piece (gp), the silver piece (sp), and the copper piece (cp).\n\nWith one gold piece, a character can buy a belt pouch, 50 feet of good rope, or a goat. A skilled (but not exceptional) artisan can earn one gold piece a day. The gold piece is the standard unit of measure for wealth, even if the coin itself is not commonly used. When merchants discuss deals that involve goods or services worth hundreds or thousands of gold pieces, the transactions don't usually involve the exchange of individual coins. Rather, the gold piece is a standard measure of value, and the actual exchange is in gold bars, letters of credit, or valuable goods.\n\nOne gold piece is worth ten silver pieces, the most prevalent coin among commoners. A silver piece buys a laborer's work for a day, a flask of lamp oil, or a night's rest in a poor inn.\n\nOne silver piece is worth ten copper pieces, which are common among laborers and beggars. A single copper piece buys a candle, a torch, or a piece of chalk.\n\nIn addition, unusual coins made of other precious metals sometimes appear in treasure hoards. The electrum piece (ep) and the platinum piece (pp) originate from fallen empires and lost kingdoms, and they sometimes arouse suspicion and skepticism when used in transactions. An electrum piece is worth five silver pieces, and a platinum piece is worth ten gold pieces.\n\nA standard coin weighs about a third of an ounce, so fifty coins weigh a pound."},
