merely a delay of death, not a denial of it, for the grave will always claim its due.\n\nNivel 3 - Grave Domain\n\nNivel 3 - Grave Domain Spells\n\nPagina: 19\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Grave Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Path to the Grave\n\nPagina: 19\n\nAs a Bonus Action, you present your Holy Symbol and expend a use of Channel Divinity to curse one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself until the start of your next turn. While cursed, the creature has XPHB on attack rolls and saving throws.\n\nWhen you or an ally you can see hits the cursed target with an attack roll, you can end the curse early (no action required) to make the attack deal extra Necrotic or Radiant damage (your choice) equal to your Cleric level.\n\nNivel 3 - Path to the Grave\n\nNivel 6 - Sentinel at Death's Door\n\nPagina: 19\n\nAt 6th level, you gain the ability to impede death's progress. As a reaction when you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you suffers a critical hit, you can turn that hit into a normal hit. Any effects triggered by a critical hit are canceled.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 6 - Sentinel at Death's Door\n\nPagina: 20\n\nWhen you or a XPHB creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself is hit with an attack roll, you can take a XPHB to halve that attack's damage (round down). If the triggering attack roll was a XPHB, any effects triggered by a XPHB are canceled.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Sentinel at Death's Door\n\nNivel 6 - Sentinel at Death's Door\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Potent Spellcasting feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Potent Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 19\n\nStarting at 8th level, you add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any cleric cantrip.\n\nNivel 17 - Divine Reaper\n\nPagina: 20\n\nYour deep connection to this domain renders you a hallowed harbinger of death, granting you the following benefits.\n\nEnhanced Necromancy\n\nWhen you cast a spell of level 5 or lower from the Necromancy school that targets one creature, or when you cast a spell from the Cleric, you can expend a use of Channel Divinity to target a second creature within the spell's range. If the spell requires costly or consumed Material components, you must provide Material components for each target.\n\nKeeper of Souls\n\nWhen an enemy dies within 60 feet of you, you or one creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself regains XPHB equal to twice your Cleric level. You can't use this feature if you have the XPHB condition. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB, unless you expend a level 6+ spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 17 - Divine Reaper\n\nNivel 17 - Keeper of Souls\n\nPagina: 19\n\nStarting at 17th level, you can seize a trace of vitality from a parting soul and use it to heal the living. When an enemy you can see dies within 60 feet of you, you or one creature of your choice that is within 60 feet of you regains hit points equal to the enemy's number of Hit Dice. You can use this feature only if you aren't incapacitated. Once you use it, you can't do so again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Keeper of Souls"},
  ["feature.grave-domain.xge2024.cleric.grave.1"]={title="Grave Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 19\n\nGods of the grave watch over the line between life and death. To these deities, death and the afterlife are a foundational part of the multiverse. To desecrate the peace of the dead is an abomination. Deities of the grave include Kelemvor, Greyhawk, the ancestral spirits of Eberron, Greek, Egyptian, and Egyptian. Followers of these deities seek to put wandering spirits to rest, destroy the undead, and ease the suffering of the dying. Their magic also allows them to stave off death for a time, particularly for a person who still has some great work to accomplish in the world. This is a delay of death, not a denial of it, for death will eventually get its due.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | bane, false life\n\n3rd | gentle repose, ray of enfeeblement\n\n5th | revivify, vampiric touch\n\n7th | blight, death ward\n\n9th | antilife shell, raise dead"},
  ["feature.grave-domain.xge2024.cleric.grave.3"]={title="Grave Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.grave-domain-spells.rhw2014.cleric.grave.3"]={title="Grave Domain Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Grave Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["spell.grave-ground.au2014"]={title="Grave Ground",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\nSkeletal hands burst from an area on the ground within range. The area consists of up to four 10-foot squares, which you arrange as you like. Each square must be contiguous with at least one other square. That area is XPHB for your enemies.\n\nAny enemy in that area when the skeletal hands appear makes a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 6d6 Necrotic damage, and until the end of its next turn, the creature subtracts 1d6 from all its damage rolls. An enemy also makes this save if it enters the area or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn."},
  ["feature.grave-power.au2014.wizard.necromancer.6"]={title="Grave Power",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nYou have discovered more necromantic insights and inscribed them in your spellbook. While holding your spellbook, you gain the following benefits.\n\nGrave Resilience\n\nWhen you use Arcane Recovery, your XPHB level, if any, decreases by 1.\n\nOverwhelming Necrosis\n\nDamage from your Wizard spells and Wizard features ignores XPHB to Necrotic damage."},
  ["magicitem.grave-reaper.au2014"]={title="Grave Reaper",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. When you hit a creature with it, the target takes an extra 2d8 Necrotic damage.\n\nSoul Lantern\n\nWhile holding this weapon, you can cast the AU spell. When you cast the spell using the weapon, the conjured lantern can hold up to five soul fragments, and the spell's save DC is 17.\n\nOnce the weapon has been used to cast the spell, it can't be used to cast it again until the next dawn."},
  ["feature.grave-touched.rhw2014.warlock.undead.6"]={title="Grave Touched",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nYour patron's powers have a profound effect on your body and magic, granting you the following benefits.\n\nArcane Necrosis\n\nNecrotic damage from your attacks, Warlock spells, and Warlock features ignores XPHB to Necrotic damage. Once per turn when you cast a spell that deals damage, you can change that spell's damage type to Necrotic.\n\nDreaded Necrosis\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll and deal Necrotic damage while using your Form of Dread, you can roll one additional damage die when determining the Necrotic damage the target takes. You can use this benefit only once per turn.\n\nUndead Endurance\n\nYou don't gain XPHB levels from XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB. In addition, you don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep."},
  ["feature.grave-touched.vrgr2014.warlock.undead.6"]={title="Grave Touched",subtitle="Caracteristica - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n6th-level Undead feature\n\nYour patron's powers have a profound effect on your body and magic. You don't need to eat, drink, or breathe.\n\nIn addition, once during each of your turns, when you hit a creature with an attack roll and roll damage against the creature, you can replace the damage type with necrotic damage. While you are using your Form of Dread, you can roll one additional damage die when determining the necrotic damage the target takes."},
  ["magicitem.gravenhollow-compass-ring.oota2014"]={title="Gravenhollow Compass Ring",subtitle="Item Magico - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis gold ring is fitted with a star ruby worth 1,000 gp. A detect magic spell reveals that the gem radiates a faint aura of divination magic. The gem's star-shaped core is a magical compass that guides the ring's wearer along the safest, shortest route to Gravenhollow."},
  ["creature.graveyard-revenant.xmm2024"]={title="Graveyard Revenant",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 260\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 161 (14d12 + 70)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 20 | INT 13 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus two other languages\n\nResistencias: necrotic, psychic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Restoration\n\nIf the revenant dies, it revives 24 hours later unless XPHB is cast on its remains. If it revives, it animates another group of corpses elsewhere on the same plane of existence; it now looks different but uses the same stat block and returns with all its XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe revenant makes two Suffocate attacks.\n\nSuffocate\n\nm 8, reach 10 ft. h10 (1d10 + 5) Bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) Necrotic damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 15). Until the grapple ends, the target is suffocating. The revenant can have up to two targets XPHB in this way at a time.\n\nHaunting Glare {@recharge 5}\n\nwis 15, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB originating from the revenant. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically."},
  ["subclass.graviturgy-magic.egw2014.wizard.graviturgy.0"]={title="Graviturgy Magic",subtitle="Subclasse - EGW - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 2 - Adjust Density\n\nPagina: 185\n\n2nd-level Graviturgy Magic feature\n\nAs an action, you can magically alter the weight of one object or creature you can see within 30 feet of you. The object or creature must be Large or smaller. The target's weight is halved or doubled for up to 1 minute or until your concentration ends (as if you were concentration on a spell).\n\nWhile the weight of a creature is halved by this effect, the creature's speed increases by 10 feet, it can jump twice as far as normal, and it has disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. While the weight of a creature is doubled by this effect, the creature's speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it has advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\n\nUpon reaching 10th level in this class, you can target an object or a creature that is Huge or smaller.\n\nNivel 2 - Adjust Density\n\nNivel 2 - Graviturgy Magic\n\nPagina: 185\n\nUnderstanding and mastering the forces that draw bodies of matter together or drive them apart, the students of the Graviturgy arcane tradition learn to further bend and manipulate the violent energy of gravity to their benefit, and the terrible detriment of their enemies.\n\n{@note Note: This subclass has access to EGW.\n\nNivel 3 - Graviturgy Magic\n\nNivel 6 - Gravity Well\n\nPagina: 185\n\n6th-level Graviturgy Magic feature\n\nYou've learned how to manipulate gravity around a living being: whenever you cast a spell on a creature, you can move the target 5 feet to an unoccupied space of your choice if the target is willing to move, the spell hits it with an attack, or it fails a saving throw against the spell.\n\nNivel 10 - Violent Attraction\n\nPagina: 185\n\n10th-level Graviturgy Magic feature\n\nWhen another creature that you can see within 60 feet of you hits with a weapon attack, you can use your reaction to increase the attack's velocity, causing the attack's target to take an extra 1d10 damage of the weapon's type.\n\nAlternatively, if a creature within 60 feet of you takes damage from a fall, you can use your reaction to increase the fall's damage by 2d10.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (a minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 10 - Violent Attraction\n\nNivel 14 - Event Horizon\n\nPagina: 185\n\n14th-level Graviturgy Magic feature\n\nAs an action, you can magically emit a powerful field of gravitational energy that tugs at other creatures for up to 1 minute or until your concentration ends (as if you were concentration on a spell). For the duration, whenever a creature hostile to you starts its turn within 30 feet of you, it must make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, it takes 2d10 force damage, and its speed is reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage, and every foot it moves this turn costs 2 extra feet of movement.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest or until you expend a spell slot of 3rd level or higher on it.\n\nNivel 14 - Event Horizon"},
  ["feature.graviturgy-magic.egw2014.wizard.graviturgy.2"]={title="Graviturgy Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\nUnderstanding and mastering the forces that draw bodies of matter together or drive them apart, the students of the Graviturgy arcane tradition learn to further bend and manipulate the violent energy of gravity to their benefit, and the terrible detriment of their enemies.\n\n{@note Note: This subclass has access to EGW."},
  ["feature.graviturgy-magic.egw2014.wizard.graviturgy.3"]={title="Graviturgy Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["spell.gravity-fissure.egw2014"]={title="Gravity Fissure",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 187\n\nYou manifest a ravine of gravitational energy in a line originating from you that is 100 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a Constitution saving throw, taking 8d8 force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nEach creature within 10 feet of the line but not in it must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 8d8 force damage and be pulled toward the line until the creature is in its area."},
  ["spell.gravity-sinkhole.egw2014"]={title="Gravity Sinkhole",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 187\n\nA 20-foot-radius sphere of crushing force forms at a point you can see within range and tugs at the creatures there. Each creature in the sphere must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 5d10 force damage and is pulled in a straight line toward the center of the sphere, ending in an unoccupied space as close to the center as possible (even if that space is in the air). On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't pulled."},
  ["feature.gravity-well.egw2014.wizard.graviturgy.6"]={title="Gravity Well",subtitle="Caracteristica - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n6th-level Graviturgy Magic feature\n\nYou've learned how to manipulate gravity around a living being: whenever you cast a spell on a creature, you can move the target 5 feet to an unoccupied space of your choice if the target is willing to move, the spell hits it with an attack, or it fails a saving throw against the spell."},
  ["creature.gray-ooze.mm2014"]={title="Gray Ooze",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 8\n\nPV: 22 (3d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 6 | CON 16 | INT 1 | WIS 6 | CHA 2\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe ooze can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nCorrode Metal\n\nAny nonmagical weapon made of metal that hits the ooze corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to −5, the weapon is destroyed. Nonmagical ammunition made of metal that hits the ooze is destroyed after dealing damage.\n\nThe ooze can eat through 2-inch-thick, nonmagical metal in 1 round.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the ooze remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an oily pool or wet rock.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPseudopod\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage, and if the target is wearing nonmagical metal armor, its armor is partly corroded and takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to the AC it offers. The armor is destroyed if the penalty reduces its AC to 10."},
  ["creature.gray-ooze.xmm2024"]={title="Gray Ooze",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 151\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 22 (3d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 6 | CON 16 | INT 1 | WIS 6 | CHA 2\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe ooze can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so.\n\nCorrosive Form\n\nNonmagical ammunition is destroyed immediately after hitting the ooze and dealing any damage. Any nonmagical weapon takes a cumulative -1 penalty to attack rolls immediately after dealing damage to the ooze and coming into contact with it. The weapon is destroyed if the penalty reaches -5. The penalty can be removed by casting the XPHB spell on the weapon.\n\nThe ooze can eat through 2-inch-thick, nonmagical metal or wood in 1 round.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPseudopod\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d8 + 1) Acid damage. Nonmagical armor worn by the target takes a -1 penalty to the AC it offers. The armor is destroyed if the penalty reduces its AC to 10. The penalty can be removed by casting the XPHB spell on the armor."},
  ["creature.gray-ooze-glob.hotb2014"]={title="Gray Ooze Glob",subtitle="Criatura - HotB - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 19 (3d6 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 6 | CON 16 | INT 1 | WIS 6 | CHA 2\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe ooze can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so.\n\nCorrosive Form\n\nWhenever a creature hits the ooze with a melee attack, that creature takes 2 Acid damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPseudopod\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d8 + 1) Acid damage."},
  ["creature.gray-render.mpmm2014"]={title="Gray Render",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 146\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 189 (18d10 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 13 | CON 20 | INT 3 | WIS 6 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gray render makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d12 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, the target must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage, plus 10 (3d6) bludgeoning damage if the target is prone.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nBloody Rampage\n\nWhen the gray render takes damage, it makes one Claw attack against a random creature within its reach, other than its master."},
  ["creature.gray-render.mtf2014"]={title="Gray Render",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 189 (18d10 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 13 | CON 20 | INT 3 | WIS 6 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gray render makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d12 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, the target must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage. If the target is prone an additional 7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage is dealt to the target.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nBloody Rampage\n\nWhen the gray render takes damage, it makes one attack with its claws against a random creature within its reach, other than its master."},
  ["creature.gray-scavver.bam2014"]={title="Gray Scavver",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 49\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 15 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe scavver doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit (with advantage if the target is a creature that is missing any hit points), reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.gray-slaad.mm2014"]={title="Gray Slaad",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 277\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 8 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Slaad, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe slaad can use its action to polymorph into a Small or Medium humanoid, or back into its true form. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe slaad's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe slaad regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe slaad makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws or greatsword.\n\nBite (Slaad Form Only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaws (Slaad Form Only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.gray-slaad.xmm2024"]={title="Gray Slaad",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 286\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 150 (20d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 8 | CHA 18\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Slaad; telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe slaad regains 10 XPHB at the start of each of its turns if it has at least 1 XPHB.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe slaad makes two Chaos Claw attacks.\n\nChaos Claw\n\nm 8, reach 10 ft. h9 (1d10 + 4) Slashing damage plus 11 (2d10) Necrotic damage. Until the start of the slaad's next turn, the target has a condition determined by rolling 1d4: on a 1, XPHB; on a 2, XPHB; on a 3, XPHB; or on a 4, XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe slaad shape-shifts into a Small or Medium Humanoid, or it returns to its true form. Other than its size, its game statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["creature.graz-zt.mpmm2014"]={title="Graz'zt",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 148\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 346 (33d10 + 165)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 15 | CON 21 | INT 23 | WIS 21 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Graz'zt fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nGraz'zt has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nGraz'zt makes two Wave of Sorrow attacks. He can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nWave of Sorrow (Greatsword)\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (4d6 + 6) force damage plus 14 (4d6) acid damage.\n\nTeleport\n\nGraz'zt teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space he can see.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nGraz'zt transforms into a form that resembles a Medium Humanoid or back into his true form. Aside from his size, his statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment he is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nNegate Spell {@recharge 5}\n\nGraz'zt tries to interrupt a spell he sees a creature casting within 60 feet of him. If the spell is 3rd level or lower, the spell fails and has no effect. If the spell is 4th level or higher, Graz'zt makes a Charisma check against a DC of 10 + the spell's level. On a success, the spell fails and has no effect.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAbyssal Magic\n\nGraz'zt uses Spellcasting or Teleport.\n\nAttack\n\nGraz'zt makes one Wave of Sorrow attack.\n\nDance, My Puppet!\n\nOne creature charmed by Graz'zt that Graz'zt can see must use its reaction to move up to its speed as Graz'zt directs."},
  ["creature.graz-zt.mtf2014"]={title="Graz'zt",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 346 (33d10 + 165)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 15 | CON 21 | INT 23 | WIS 21 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nGraz'zt can use his action to polymorph into a form that resembles a Medium humanoid, or back into his true form. Aside from his size, his statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment he is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Graz'zt fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nGraz'zt has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nGraz'zt's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nGraz'zt attacks twice with Wave of Sorrow.\n\nWave of Sorrow (Greatsword)\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (4d6 + 6) slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) acid damage.\n\nTeleport\n\nGraz'zt magically teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space he can see.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nGraz'zt attacks once with Wave of Sorrow.\n\nDance, My Puppet\n\nOne creature charmed by Graz'zt that Graz'zt can see must use its reaction to move up to its speed as Graz'zt directs.\n\nSow Discord\n\nGraz'zt casts crown of madness or dissonant whispers.\n\nTeleport\n\nGraz'zt uses his Teleport action."},
  ["creature.grazilaxx.oota2014"]={title="Grazilaxx",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 18"},
  ["spell.grease.phb2014"]={title="Grease",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 246\n\nSlick grease covers the ground in a 10-foot square centered on a point within range and turns it into difficult terrain for the duration.\n\nWhen the grease appears, each creature standing in its area must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or fall prone. A creature that enters the area or ends its turn there must also succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or fall prone."},
  ["spell.grease.xphb2024"]={title="Grease",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 280\n\nNonflammable grease covers the ground in a 10-foot square centered on a point within range and turns it into XPHB for the duration.\n\nWhen the grease appears, each creature standing in its area must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition. A creature that enters the area or ends its turn there must also succeed on that save or fall XPHB."},
  ["creature.great-cat.psz2014"]={title="Great Cat",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.great-chief-halric-bonesnapper.skt2014"]={title="Great Chief Halric Bonesnapper",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nPV: 99 (9d8 + 27)\n\nIdiomas: Bothii, Common\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGreataxe +1\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d12 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.great-kroom-purple-worm.awm2014"]={title="Great Kroom, Purple Worm",subtitle="Criatura - AWM - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / G\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe worm can burrow through solid rock at half its burrow speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe worm makes two attacks:\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, one target. h22 (3d8) piercing damage. Target must make a 19 Dexterity save, or be swallowed by the worm!\n\nTail Stinger\n\nmw 14 to hit, one creature. h19 (3d6 + 9) piercing damage Target must make a 19 Constitution save, or take 42 (12d6) poison damage."},
  ["subclass.great-old-one-patron.xphb2024.warlock.great-old-one.0"]={title="Great Old One Patron",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 162\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Awakened Mind\n\nPagina: 109\n\nStarting at 1st level, your alien knowledge gives you the ability to touch the minds of other creatures. You can telepathically speak to any creature you can see within 30 feet of you. You don't need to share a language with the creature for it to understand your telepathic utterances, but the creature must be able to understand at least one language.\n\nNivel 1 - Awakened Mind\n\nNivel 1 - The Great Old One\n\nPagina: 109\n\nYour patron is a mysterious entity whose nature is utterly foreign to the fabric of reality. It might come from the Far Realm, the space beyond reality, or it could be one of the elder gods known only in legends. Its motives are incomprehensible to mortals, and its knowledge so immense and ancient that even the greatest libraries pale in comparison to the vast secrets it holds. The Great Old One might be unaware of your existence or entirely indifferent to you, but the secrets you have learned allow you to draw your magic from it. Entities of this type include Ghaunadar, called That Which Lurks; Tharizdun, the Chained God; Dendar, the Night Serpent; Zargon, the Returner; Great Cthulhu; and other unfathomable beings.\n\nExpanded Spell List\n\nThe Great Old One lets you choose from an expanded list of spells when you learn a warlock spell. The following spells are added to the warlock spell list for you.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1st | dissonant whispers, Tasha's hideous laughter\n\n2nd | detect thoughts, phantasmal force\n\n3rd | clairvoyance, sending\n\n4th | dominate beast, Evard's black tentacles\n\n5th | dominate person, telekinesis\n\nNivel 3 - Awakened Mind\n\nPagina: 162\n\nYou can form a telepathic connection between your mind and the mind of another. As a XPHB, choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself. You and the chosen creature can communicate telepathically with each other while the two of you are within a number of miles of each other equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 mile). To understand each other, you each must mentally use a language the other knows.\n\nThe telepathic connection lasts for a number of minutes equal to your Warlock level. It ends early if you use this feature to connect with a different creature.\n\nNivel 3 - Awakened Mind\n\nNivel 3 - Great Old One Patron\n\nPagina: 162\n\nUnearth Forbidden Lore of Ineffable Beings\n\nWhen you choose this subclass, you might bind yourself to an unspeakable being from the Far Realm or an elder god—a being such as Tharizdun, the Chained God; Zargon, the Returner; Hadar, the Dark Hunger; or Great Cthulhu. Or you might invoke several entities without yoking yourself to one. The motives of these beings are incomprehensible, and the Great Old One might be indifferent to your existence. But the secrets you've learned nevertheless allow you to draw strange magic from it.\n\nNivel 3 - Great Old One Spells\n\nPagina: 163\n\nThe magic of your patron ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Warlock level specified in the Great Old One Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nWarlock Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Psychic Spells\n\nPagina: 163\n\nWhen you cast a Warlock spell that deals damage, you can change its damage type to Psychic. In addition, when you cast a Warlock spell that is an spells or spells, you can do so without Verbal or Somatic components.\n\nNivel 3 - The Great Old One\n\nNivel 6 - Clairvoyant Combatant\n\nPagina: 163\n\nWhen you form a telepathic bond with a creature using your Awakened Mind, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, the creature has XPHB on attack rolls against you, and you have XPHB on attack rolls against that creature for the duration of the bond.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB unless you expend a Pact Magic spell slot (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 6 - Clairvoyant Combatant\n\nNivel 6 - Entropic Ward\n\nPagina: 109\n\nAt 6th level, you learn to magically ward yourself against attack and to turn an enemy's failed strike into good luck for yourself. When a creature makes an attack roll against you, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on that roll. If the attack misses you, your next attack roll against the creature has advantage if you make it before the end of your next turn.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nNivel 10 - Eldritch Hex\n\nPagina: 163\n\nYour alien patron grants you a powerful curse. You always have the XPHB spell prepared. When you cast XPHB and choose an ability, the target also has XPHB on saving throws of the chosen ability for the duration of the spell.\n\nNivel 10 - Thought Shield\n\nPagina: 109\n\nStarting at 10th level, your thoughts can't be read by telepathy or other means unless you allow it. You also have resistance to psychic damage, and whenever a creature deals psychic damage to you, that creature takes the same amount of damage that you do.\n\nNivel 10 - Thought Shield\n\nPagina: 163\n\nYour thoughts can't be read by telepathy or other means unless you allow it. You also have XPHB to Psychic damage, and whenever a creature deals Psychic damage to you, that creature takes the same amount of damage that you take.\n\nNivel 10 - Thought Shield\n\nNivel 10 - Thought Shield\n\nNivel 14 - Create Thrall\n\nPagina: 109\n\nAt 14th level, you gain the ability to infect a humanoid's mind with the alien magic of your patron. You can use your action to touch an incapacitated humanoid. That creature is then charmed by you until a remove curse spell is cast on it, the charmed condition is removed from it, or you use this feature again.\n\nYou can communicate telepathically with the charmed creature as long as the two of you are on the same plane of existence.\n\nNivel 14 - Create Thrall\n\nPagina: 163\n\nWhen you cast XPHB, you can modify it so that it doesn't require XPHB. If you do so, the spell's duration becomes 1 minute for that casting, and when summoned, the Aberration has a number of XPHB equal to your Warlock level plus your Charisma modifier.\n\nIn addition, the first time each turn the Aberration hits a creature under the effect of your XPHB, the Aberration deals extra Psychic damage to the target equal to the bonus damage of that spell.\n\nNivel 14 - Create Thrall"},
  ["feature.great-old-one-patron.xphb2024.warlock.great-old-one.3"]={title="Great Old One Patron",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 162\n\nUnearth Forbidden Lore of Ineffable Beings\n\nWhen you choose this subclass, you might bind yourself to an unspeakable being from the Far Realm or an elder god—a being such as Tharizdun, the Chained God; Zargon, the Returner; Hadar, the Dark Hunger; or Great Cthulhu. Or you might invoke several entities without yoking yourself to one. The motives of these beings are incomprehensible, and the Great Old One might be indifferent to your existence. But the secrets you've learned nevertheless allow you to draw strange magic from it."},
  ["feature.great-old-one-spells.xphb2024.warlock.great-old-one.3"]={title="Great Old One Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 163\n\nThe magic of your patron ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Warlock level specified in the Great Old One Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nWarlock Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["feature.great-stature.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.10"]={title="Great Stature",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n10th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nThe magic of your runes permanently alters you. When you gain this feature, roll 3d4. You grow a number of inches in height equal to the roll.\n\nMoreover, the extra damage you deal with your Giant's Might feature increases to 1d8."},
  ["creature.great-ulfe.tftyp2014"]={title="Great Ulfe",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["optionalfeature.great-weapon-fighting.phb2014"]={title="Great Weapon Fighting",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nWhen you roll a 1 or 2 on a damage die for an attack you make with a melee weapon that you are wielding with two hands, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll, even if the new roll is a 1 or a 2. The weapon must have the two-handed or versatile property for you to gain this benefit."},
  ["feat.great-weapon-fighting.xphb2024"]={title="Great Weapon Fighting",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 209\n\nWhen you roll damage for an attack you make with a Melee weapon that you are holding with two hands, you can treat any 1 or 2 on a damage die as a 3. The weapon must have the XPHB or XPHB property to gain this benefit."},
  ["feat.great-weapon-master.phb2014"]={title="Great Weapon Master",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\nYou've learned to put the weight of a weapon to your advantage, letting its momentum empower your strikes. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• On your turn, when you score a critical hit with a melee weapon or reduce a creature to 0 hit points with one, you can make one melee weapon attack as a bonus action.\n\n• Before you make a melee attack with a heavy weapon that you are proficient with, you can choose to take a -5 penalty to the attack roll. If the attack hits, you add +10 to the attack's damage."},
  ["feat.great-weapon-master.xphb2024"]={title="Great Weapon Master",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 204\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nHeavy Weapon Mastery\n\nWhen you hit a creature with a weapon that has the XPHB property as part of the XPHB action on your turn, you can cause the weapon to deal extra damage to the target. The extra damage equals your XPHB.\n\nHew\n\nImmediately after you score a XPHB with a Melee weapon or reduce a creature to 0 XPHB with one, you can make one attack with the same weapon as a XPHB."},
  ["item.greataxe.phb2014"]={title="Greataxe",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.greataxe.xphb2024"]={title="Greataxe",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.greatclub.phb2014"]={title="Greatclub",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.greatclub.xphb2024"]={title="Greatclub",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["feat.greater-aberrant-mark.efa2014"]={title="Greater Aberrant Mark",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Fortitude\n\nWhen you use the Aberrant Fortitude benefit of your Aberrant Dragonmark feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4. You also now regain your use of Aberrant Fortitude whenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB.\n\nMark of Inspiration\n\nWhen you cast a cantrip, you can roll one or two of your unexpended XPHB. You gain a number of XPHB equal to the number rolled plus your Constitution modifier, and one creature of your choice within 30 feet of you (not including you) takes Force damage equal to the number rolled. Those dice are then expended.\n\nYou can use this benefit a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["creature.greater-death-dragon.dsotdq2014"]={title="Greater Death Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 195\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 230 (20d12 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: piercing\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) necrotic damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 19). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the dragon can't bite a different target.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft. one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nCataclysmic Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of ghostly purple flames in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 45 (10d8) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature dies if the breath reduces it to 0 hit points. Additionally, any Medium or smaller Humanoid killed by the breath's damage, as well as every corpse of such a creature within the cone, becomes a zombie (see the Monster Manual) under the dragon's control. The zombie acts on the dragon's initiative but immediately after the dragon's turn. Absent any other command, the zombie tries to kill any non-Undead creature it encounters.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nCataclysmic Rush (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its flying speed without provoking opportunity attacks, carrying with it any creatures it is grappling. During this move, if it enters the space of a Medium or smaller creature, that creature takes 4 (1d8) necrotic damage. A creature can take this damage only once per turn."},
  ["feature.greater-divine-intervention.xphb2024.cleric.base.20"]={title="Greater Divine Intervention",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["spell.greater-invisibility.phb2014"]={title="Greater Invisibility",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 246\n\nYou or a creature you touch becomes invisible until the spell ends. Anything the target is wearing or carrying is invisible as long as it is on the target's person."},
  ["spell.greater-invisibility.xphb2024"]={title="Greater Invisibility",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 281\n\nA creature you touch has the XPHB condition until the spell ends."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-detection.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Detection",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Deductive Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nShared Detection\n\nWhen you use the Magical Detection benefit of your EFA feat to cast XPHB without a spell slot, you can choose one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself. That creature also gains the benefits of the spell for its duration."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-finding.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Finding",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Hunter's Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Finding\n\nWhen you use the Finder's Magic benefit of your EFA to cast XPHB without a spell slot, the range of the spell is doubled, and you can modify the spell so that the target can't benefit from the XPHB condition for the duration."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-handling.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Handling",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Wild Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Handling\n\nWhile you are mounted, immediately after you hit a target within 5 feet of your mount with a melee attack roll, your mount can take a XPHB to move up to its XPHB or take the XPHB action to make one attack only (your choice).\n\nSubdue Animal\n\nAs a XPHB action, you exert command over one Beast or Monstrosity you can see within 30 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 plus your Wisdom modifier and XPHB) or have the XPHB condition until the start of your next turn. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-healing.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Healing",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Medical Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Healing\n\nYou can now use the Healing Touch benefit of your EFA feat to cast XPHB without using a spell slot a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB. Additionally, when you cast XPHB and roll dice to determine the number of XPHB restored, you can treat any 1 or 2 on a roll as a 3."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-hospitality.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Hospitality",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Ever Hospitable benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Hospitality\n\nWhen you cast XPHB, you can modify the spell so that instead of its normal effect, each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you is refreshed. Each affected creature's XPHB level is reduced by 1, and the creature gains XPHB equal to your XPHB plus your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma modifier (choose when you select this feat). Once you modify the spell with this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-making.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Making",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Artisan's Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Making\n\nWhen you use the Spellsmith benefit of your EFA feat to cast XPHB without a spell slot, you cast the spell as its level 3 version."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-passage.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Passage",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Intuitive Motion benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Passage\n\nWhen you use the Magical Passage benefit of your EFA feat to cast XPHB without a spell slot, you can also choose up to two willing creatures you can see within 30 feet of yourself before you teleport. Each target can then take a XPHB to also teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-scribing.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Scribing",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Gifted Scribe benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nInspired Scribing\n\nWhen you cast XPHB, you can modify the spell to encompass up to three willing creatures you can see within 30 feet of yourself. Each chosen creature also gains the benefits of the spell for the duration. In addition, for the duration of the spell, you and the chosen creatures can communicate telepathically with each other while within 1 mile of each other. Once you modify the spell with this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-sentinel.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Sentinel",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Sentinel's Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Sentinel\n\nWhen you use the Vigilant Guardian benefit of your EFA feat, you can also make one attack with a weapon or an XPHB as part of that same XPHB."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-shadow.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Shadow",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Cunning Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Shadow\n\nWhen you use the Shape Shadows benefit of your EFA feat to cast XPHB without a spell slot, you cast the spell as its level 3 version."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-storm.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Storm",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Windwright's Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Storm\n\nWhen you use the Storm Magic benefit of your EFA feat to cast XPHB without a spell slot, you also gain a XPHB of 60 feet for the duration of the spell."},
  ["feat.greater-mark-of-warding.efa2014"]={title="Greater Mark of Warding",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Intuition\n\nWhen you use the Warder's Intuition benefit of your EFA feat, you can roll 1d6 instead of 1d4.\n\nImproved Warding\n\nWhen a creature makes an attack roll against you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself, you can take a XPHB to impose XPHB on that roll. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feature.greater-portent.phb2014.wizard.divination.14"]={title="Greater Portent",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nStarting at 14th level, the visions in your dreams intensify and paint a more accurate picture in your mind of what is to come. You roll three d20s for your Portent feature, rather than two."},
  ["feature.greater-portent.xphb2024.wizard.diviner.14"]={title="Greater Portent",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 173\n\nThe visions in your dreams intensify and paint a more accurate picture in your mind of what is to come. Roll three d20s for your Portent feature rather than two."},
  ["spell.greater-restoration.phb2014"]={title="Greater Restoration",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 246\n\nYou imbue a creature you touch with positive energy to undo a debilitating effect. You can reduce the target's exhaustion level by one, or end one of the following effects on the target:\n\n• One effect that charmed or petrified the target\n\n• One curse, including the target's attunement to a cursed magic item\n\n• Any reduction to one of the target's ability scores\n\n• One effect reducing the target's hit point maximum"},
  ["spell.greater-restoration.xphb2024"]={title="Greater Restoration",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 281\n\nYou touch a creature and magically remove one of the following effects from it:\n\n• 1 XPHB level\n\n• The XPHB or XPHB condition\n\n• A curse, including the target's XPHB to a cursed magic item\n\n• Any reduction to one of the target's ability scores\n\n• Any reduction to the target's XPHB maximum"},
  ["creature.greater-shadow-horror.aitfr-thp2014"]={title="Greater Shadow Horror",subtitle="Criatura - AitFR-THP - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / H\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 170 (20d12 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nVulnerabilidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe horror can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the horror fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the horror can take the Hide action as a bonus action.\n\nShadow Stride\n\nAs a bonus action, the horror can step into a shadow within 5 feet of it and magically appear in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of a second shadow that is up to 60 feet away. Both shadows must be cast by a Medium or larger creature or object.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the horror has disadvantage on attack rolls and on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe horror makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h21 (4d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (4d6 + 3) slashing damage, and the target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened of the horror until the end of the target's next turn.\n\nLashing Shadows {@recharge 5}\n\nEach creature within 60 feet of the horror, except other horrors, must succeed on a 16 Dexterity saving throw or take 36 (8d8) necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe horror makes a weapon attack.\n\nGlide\n\nThe horror moves up to 20 feet without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nFrighten Foe (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe horror targets one enemy it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see and hear it, the target must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of horror's next turn."},
  ["magicitem.greater-silver-sword.mtf2014"]={title="Greater Silver Sword",subtitle="Item Magico - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis magic weapon grants a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. While you hold the sword, you have advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws, you are immune to being charmed, and you have resistance to psychic damage. In addition, if you score a critical hit with it against a creature's astral body, you can cut the silvery cord that tethers the target to its material body, instead of dealing damage."},
  ["creature.greater-star-spawn-emissary.rhw2014"]={title="Greater Star Spawn Emissary",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / H\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 304 (21d12 + 168)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 13 | CON 26 | INT 27 | WIS 22 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, force, necrotic, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAberrant Restoration\n\nIf destroyed, the emissary revives with all its XPHB in 1 day in the space of a Gibbering Mouther that was within 300 feet of the emissary when the emissary was destroyed; that mouther is destroyed.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the emissary fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe emissary makes two attacks, using Lashing Maw or Coagulated Nodule in any combination. It can replace one attack with Unearthly Bile if available.\n\nLashing Maw\n\nm 14, reach 15 ft. h33 (4d12 + 7) Piercing damage plus 18 (4d8) Acid damage.\n\nCoagulated Nodule\n\nr 15, range 120 ft. h44 (8d8 + 8) Acid damage.\n\nUnearthly Bile {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 23, each creature in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the emissary can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 54 (12d8) Acid damage, and a Gibbering Mouther appears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of the target. The mouthers take their turn immediately after the emissary on the same XPHB count. Each mouther fights until destroyed. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nForced Mutations\n\ncha 23, up to two creatures the emissary can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The emissary can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nTeleporting Lash\n\nThe emissary can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see, and it makes one Lashing Maw attack."},
  ["creature.greater-star-spawn-emissary.vrgr2014"]={title="Greater Star Spawn Emissary",subtitle="Criatura - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / H\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 290 (20d12 + 160)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 13 | CON 26 | INT 27 | WIS 22 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 1,000 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, force, necrotic, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the emissary fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe emissary doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe emissary makes three attacks.\n\nLashing Maw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 7) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) acid damage.\n\nPsychic Orb\n\nrs 15 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h27 (3d12 + 8) psychic damage.\n\nUnearthly Bile {@recharge 5}\n\nThe emissary expels bile that splashes all creatures in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point within 120 feet of the emissary. Each creature in that area must make a 23 Dexterity saving throw, taking 55 (10d10) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. For each creature that fails the saving throw, a gibbering mouther (see its entry in the Monster Manual) appears in an unoccupied space on a surface that can support it within 30 feet of that creature. The gibbering mouthers act right after the emissary on the same initiative count, gaining a +7 bonus to their attack and damage rolls, and fighting until they are destroyed. They disappear when the emissary dies.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe emissary teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see and makes one attack.\n\nWarp Space (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe emissary causes the ground in a 20-foot square that it can see within 90 feet of it to turn into teeth and maws until the start of its next turn. The area becomes difficult terrain for the duration. Any creature takes 10 (3d6) piercing damage for each 5 feet it moves on this terrain.\n\nMind Cloud (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe emissary unleashes a psychic wave. Each creature within 30 feet of the emissary must succeed on a 23 Wisdom saving throw or take 32 (5d12) psychic damage. In addition, every spell ends on creatures and objects of the emissary's choice in that area."},
  ["creature.greater-tyrant-shadow.coa2014"]={title="Greater Tyrant Shadow",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 256\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 372 (24d20 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 15 | CON 20 | INT 24 | WIS 16 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands all, telepathy 300 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEmpath\n\nThe shadow uses telepathy to sense nearby creatures. The shadow can see a creature if that creature has thoughts and is within the range of the shadow's telepathy. The shadow can't see creatures immune to telepathy.\n\nUndying Connection\n\nThe shadow was originally spawned from a specific devil and, if the shadow is slain, it returns to life in 10 (1d20) days within 1 mile of that devil. The shadow is killed permanently only if its progenitor devil is slain first.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe shadow makes three Claw attacks. It can replace one of the attacks with Shadows of Death (if available).\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h21 (4d6 + 7) necrotic damage, plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage.\n\nCloak of Shadows\n\nThe shadow bends darkness around itself, and now has the invisible condition for 1 minute. The invisibility ends if the shadow is subjected to a Daylight spell or similar.\n\nEmpathic Link\n\nThe shadow attempts to form a link between itself and a creature it can see. The target must make a 22 Intelligence saving throw, taking 26 (4d12) psychic damage on a success. On a failed save, the creature and the shadow are linked. While linked, every time the shadow is damaged, the creature takes half of that damage as psychic damage. The creature may repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, taking 26 (4d12) psychic damage on a failed save, or ending the effect on a successful one.\n\nShadows of Death {@recharge 5}\n\nThe shadow discharges inky-black shadows in a 90-foot-radius sphere around itself. Creatures in the shadows must succeed on a 22 Wisdom saving throw or take 36 (8d8) necrotic damage and have the frightened condition for 1 minute. A frightened creature may repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a successful save, but taking the damage again on a failed save.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe shadow transforms into a Beast, Humanoid or Fiend that it has an Empathic Link with, or back into its true form. In a new form, the shadow retains its alignment, hit points, hit dice, telepathy, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features, lair actions, or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nShadow Blink\n\nThe shadow surrounds itself in black mist, then teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space that it can see.\n\nShapeshift\n\nThe shadow uses its Change Shape ability.\n\nMind Spike (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nrs 14 to hit, range 300 ft., one target. h23 (3d10 + 7) psychic damage."},
  ["creature.greater-zombie.tftyp2014"]={title="Greater Zombie",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 97 (13d8 + 39)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 4 | WIS 6 | CHA 6\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages it knew in life but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTurn Resistance\n\nThe zombie has advantage on saving throws against any effect that turns undead.\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the zombie to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 + the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the zombie drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe zombie makes two melee attacks.\n\nEmpowered Slam\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage and 7 (2d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["item.greatsword.phb2014"]={title="Greatsword",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.greatsword.xphb2024"]={title="Greatsword",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.green-abishai.mpmm2014"]={title="Green Abishai",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 195 (26d8 + 78)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the abishai's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe abishai has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe abishai makes two Fiendish Claw attacks, or it makes one Fiendish Claw attack and uses Spellcasting.\n\nFiendish Claw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) force damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or take 16 (3d10) poison damage and become poisoned for 1 minute. The poisoned target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.green-abishai.mtf2014"]={title="Green Abishai",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 162\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 187 (25d8 + 75)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the abishai's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe abishai has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe abishai's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe abishai makes two attacks, one with its claws and one with its longsword, or it casts one spell from its Innate Spellcasting trait and makes one claw attack.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) slashing damage, or 6 (1d10 + 1) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or take 11 (2d10) poison damage and become poisoned for 1 minute. The poisoned target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["magicitem.green-chromatic-rose.wbtw2014"]={title="Green Chromatic Rose",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\n{#itemEntry Chromatic Rose|WBtW"},
  ["magicitem.green-copper-ewer.cos2014"]={title="Green Copper Ewer",subtitle="Item Magico - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 188\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nAny poisonous liquid poured into the ewer is instantly transformed into an equal amount of sweet wine. Furthermore, a creature that grasps the ewer's handle can command the ewer to fill with 1 gallon of wine, and it can't produce more wine until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.green-dragon-mask.rotos2014"]={title="Green Dragon Mask",subtitle="Item Magico - RoTOS - 2014",body="Pagina: 4\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis mottled green mask is surmounted by a frilled crest and has leathery spiked plates along its jaw. The mask reshapes to fit a wearer attuned to it. While you are wearing the mask and attuned to it, you can access the following properties\n\nDamage Absorption\n\nYou have resistance against poison damage. If you already have resistance to poison damage from another source, you instead have immunity to poison damage. If you already have immunity to poison damage from another source, whenever you are subjected to poison damage, you take none of that damage and regain a number of hit points equal to half the damage dealt of that type.\n\nDraconic Majesty\n\nWhile you are wearing no armor, you can add your Charisma bonus to your Armor Class.\n\nDragon Breath\n\nIf you have a breath weapon that requires rest to recharge, it gains a recharge of 6.\n\nDragon Sight\n\nYou gain darkvision out to 60 feet, or to an additional 60 feet if you already have that sense. Once per day, you can gain blindsight out to 30 feet for 5 minutes.\n\nDragon Tongue\n\nYou can speak and understand Draconic. You also have advantage on any Charisma check you make against Green Dragons.\n\nLegendary Resistance\n\n(1/Day) If you fail a saving throw, you can choose to succeed instead.\n\nWater Breathing\n\nYou can breathe underwater."},
  ["magicitem.green-dragon-scale-mail.dmg2014"]={title="Green Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nDragon scale mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them to humanoids. Other times, hunters carefully skin and preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, dragon scale mail is highly valued. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, you have advantage on saving throws against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of dragons, and you have resistance to poison damage.\n\nAdditionally, you can focus your senses as an action to magically discern the distance and direction to the closest green dragon within 30 miles of you. This special action can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.green-dragon-scale-mail.xdmg2024"]={title="Green Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 254\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\n{#itemEntry Dragon Scale Mail|XDMG"},
  ["creature.green-dragon-wyrmling.mm2014"]={title="Green Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) poison damage.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales poisonous gas in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 11 Constitution saving throw, taking 21 (6d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.green-dragon-wyrmling.xmm2024"]={title="Green Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 152\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 10 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d10 + 2) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage.\n\nPoison Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 11, each creature in a 15-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 21 (6d6) Poison damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.green-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Green Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 27\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 533 (26d20 + 260)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 14 | CON 30 | INT 21 | WIS 20 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChromatic Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 425 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use the options in the \"Mythic Actions\" section for 1 hour. Award a party an additional 105,000 XP (210,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Chromatic Awakening activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 20) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled this way at a time.\n\nTail\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm exhales a blast of energy in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 26 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 78 (12d12) poison damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw or Tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm beats its wings. Each creature within 30 feet of it must succeed on a 26 Dexterity saving throw or take 17 (2d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The greatwyrm can then fly up to half its flying speed.\n\nArcane Spear (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm creates four spears of magical force. Each spear hits a creature of the greatwyrm's choice it can see within 120 feet of it, dealing 12 (1d8 + 8) force damage to its target, then disappears.\n\n=== ACOES MITICAS ===\n\nBite\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack.\n\nChromatic Flare (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm flares with elemental energy. Each creature in a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on the greatwyrm must succeed on a 26 Dexterity saving throw or take 22 (5d8) poison damage."},
  ["creature.green-guard-drake.vgm2014"]={title="Green Guard Drake",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (7d8 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 16 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak it\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe guard drake can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe drake attacks twice, once with its bite and once with its tail.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.green-hag.mm2014"]={title="Green Hag",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 177\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe hag can breathe air and water.\n\nMimicry\n\nThe hag can mimic animal sounds and humanoid voices. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations with a successful 14 Wisdom (Insight) check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nIllusory Appearance\n\nThe hag covers herself and anything she is wearing or carrying with a magical illusion that makes her look like another creature of her general size and humanoid shape. The illusion ends if the hag takes a bonus action to end it or if she dies.\n\nThe changes wrought by this effect fail to hold up to physical inspection. For example, the hag could appear to have smooth skin, but someone touching her would feel her rough flesh. Otherwise, a creature must take an action to visually inspect the illusion and succeed on a 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the hag is disguised.\n\nInvisible Passage\n\nThe hag magically turns invisible until she attacks or casts a spell, or until her concentration ends (as if concentration on a spell). While invisible, she leaves no physical evidence of her passage, so she can be tracked only by magic. Any equipment she wears or carries is invisible with her."},
  ["creature.green-hag.xmm2024"]={title="Green Hag",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 156\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe hag can breathe air and water.\n\nMimicry\n\nThe hag can mimic animal sounds and humanoid voices. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations only with a successful 14 Wisdom (XPHB) check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nCoven Magic\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe hag makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."},
  ["creature.green-slaad.mm2014"]={title="Green Slaad",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 277\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 127 (15d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 8 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Slaad, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe slaad can use its action to polymorph into a Small or Medium humanoid, or back into its true form. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe slaad regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe slaad makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws or staff. Alternatively, it uses its Hurl Flame twice.\n\nBite (Slaad Form Only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaw (Slaad Form Only)\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nStaff\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nHurl Flame\n\nrs 4 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) fire damage. The fire ignites flammable objects that aren't being worn or carried."},
  ["creature.green-slaad.xmm2024"]={title="Green Slaad",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 286\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 144 (17d10 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 8 | CHA 18\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Slaad; telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe slaad regains 10 XPHB at the start of each of its turns if it has at least 1 XPHB.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe slaad makes three Chaos Staff attacks.\n\nChaos Staff\n\nm,r 7, reach 10 ft. or range 60 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Force damage. Until the start of the slaad's next turn, the target has a condition determined by rolling 1d4: on a 1, XPHB; on a 2, XPHB; on a 3, XPHB; or on a 4, XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe slaad shape-shifts into a Small or Medium Humanoid, or it returns to its true form. Other than its size, its game statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["traphazard.green-slime.dmg2014"]={title="Green Slime",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\nThis acidic slime devours flesh, organic material, and metal on contact. Bright green, wet, and sticky, it clings to walls, floors, and ceilings in patches.\n\nA patch of green slime covers a 5-foot square, has blindsight out to a range of 30 feet, and drops from walls and ceilings when it detects movement below it. Beyond that, it has no ability to move. A creature aware of the slime's presence can avoid being struck by it with a successful 10 Dexterity saving throw. Otherwise, the slime can't be avoided as it drops.\n\nA creature that comes into contact with green slime takes 5 (1d10) acid damage. The creature takes the damage again at the start of each of its turns until the slime is scraped off or destroyed. Against wood or metal, green slime deals 11 (2d10) acid damage each round, and any nonmagical wood or metal weapon or tool used to scrape off the slime is effectively destroyed.\n\nSunlight, any effect that cures disease, and any effect that deals cold, fire, or radiant damage destroys a patch of green slime."},
  ["traphazard.green-slime.xdmg2024"]={title="Green Slime",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 76\n\nAcidic green slime devours flesh, organic material, and metal on contact. Bright green, wet, and sticky, it clings to walls, floors, and ceilings in patches.\n\nOne patch of green slime covers a 5-foot square. Green slime has XPHB with a range of 30 feet, and it drops from walls and ceilings when it detects movement below itself. Beyond that, it can't move. A creature aware of the slime's presence can avoid being struck by it with a successful 10 Dexterity saving throw.\n\nA creature that comes in contact with green slime takes 5 (1d10) Acid damage. The creature takes the damage again at the start of each of its turns until the slime is scraped off (requiring an action) or destroyed. Against wood or metal, green slime deals 11 (2d10) Acid damage each round, and any nonmagical wood or metal item used to scrape off the green slime is destroyed.\n\nDirect sunlight or any amount of Cold, Fire, or Radiant damage destroys a patch of green slime."},
  ["spell.green-flame-blade.tce2014"]={title="Green-Flame Blade",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 107\n\nYou brandish the weapon used in the spell's casting and make a melee attack with it against one creature within 5 feet of you. On a hit, the target suffers the weapon attack's normal effects, and you can cause green fire to leap from the target to a different creature of your choice that you can see within 5 feet of it. The second creature takes fire damage equal to your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\nThis spell's damage increases when you reach certain levels. At 5th level, the melee attack deals an extra 1d8 fire damage to the target on a hit, and the fire damage to the second creature increases to 1d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier. Both damage rolls increase by 1d8 at 11th level (2d8 and 2d8) and 17th level (3d8 and 3d8)."},
  ["creature.gregir-fendelsohn-levels-1-4.kftgv2014"]={title="Gregir Fendelsohn (Levels 1-4)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.gregir-fendelsohn-levels-5-8.kftgv2014"]={title="Gregir Fendelsohn (Levels 5-8)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.gregir-fendelsohn-levels-9-11.kftgv2014"]={title="Gregir Fendelsohn (Levels 9-11)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.grell.mm2014"]={title="Grell",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 172\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 55 (10d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Grell\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, prone\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grell makes two attacks: one with its tentacles and one with its beak.\n\nTentacles\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute. The poisoned target is paralyzed, and it can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.\n\nThe target is also grappled (escape 15). If the target is Medium or smaller, it is also restrained until this grapple ends. While grappling the target, the grell has advantage on attack rolls against it and can't use this attack against other targets. When the grell moves, any Medium or smaller target it is grappling moves with it.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["language.grell.mm2014"]={title="Grell",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 172"},
  ["creature.grell.xmm2024"]={title="Grell",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 157\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 55 (10d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAbduct\n\nThe grell needn't spend extra movement to move a creature it is grappling.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grell makes one Beak attack and one Paralyzing Tentacles attack.\n\nBeak\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d8 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\nParalyzing Tentacles\n\nm 4, reach 10 ft. h7 (1d10 + 2) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 12) from two of ten tentacles. The target is also subjected to the following effect. con 11. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.grell-psychic.pabtso2014"]={title="Grell Psychic",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, Grell\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, prone\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grell psychic makes one Tentacle attack and one Beak attack.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (3d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or have the poisoned condition for 1 minute. While the target is poisoned, it also has the paralyzed condition. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The target also has the grappled condition (escape 16). While grappling the target, the grell can't make Tentacle attacks against other targets. When the grell moves, any Medium or smaller target it is grappling moves with it."},
  ["creature.gremishka.rhw2014"]={title="Gremishka",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 249\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / T\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 31 (7d4 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe gremishka has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite (Individual Form Only)\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Force damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nMagic Allergy (Individual Form Only; 1/Day)\n\nactTrigger A creature within 30 feet of the gremishka casts a spell. actResponse The gremishka regains 15 XPHB, then becomes a RHW."},
  ["creature.gremishka.vrgr2014"]={title="Gremishka",subtitle="Criatura - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 235\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / T\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 10 (4d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) force damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nMagic Allergy (1/Day)\n\nImmediately after a creature within 30 feet of the gremishka casts a spell, the gremishka can spontaneously react to the magic. Roll a d6 to determine the effect:\n\n• 1-2\n\n• 3-4\n\n• 5-6"},
  ["creature.gremlin.psk2014"]={title="Gremlin",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 13 | CON 13 | INT 3 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAether Scent\n\nThe gremlin can pinpoint, by scent, the location of refined or unrefined aether within 30 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) slashing damage.\n\nSiphon\n\nThe gremlin drains aether from an aether-powered device it can see within 5 feet of it. If the object isn't being worn or carried, the touch automatically drains aether. If the object is being worn or carried by a creature, the creature must succeed on a 11 Dexterity saving throw to keep it out of the gremlin's reach.\n\nIf the aether-powered device grants any bonus (to attack rolls, damage rolls, Armor Class, and so on), that bonus is reduced by 1. If the device has charges, it loses 1 charge. Otherwise, it stops functioning for 1 round. Left unhindered, a gremlin can completely destroy an aether-powered device."},
  ["creature.gremorly-s-ghost.bmt2014"]={title="Gremorly's Ghost",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 82 (15d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 18 | WIS 12 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Giant\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEthereal Sight\n\nGremorly can see 60 feet into the Ethereal Plane when he is on the Material Plane, and vice versa.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nGremorly can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. He takes 5 (1d10) force damage if he ends his turn inside an object.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Gremorly fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nGremorly makes three Withering Strike attacks.\n\nWithering Strike\n\nms 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (3d12) necrotic damage.\n\nFell Necromancy\n\nGremorly targets one creature he can see within 60 feet of himself. The target must make a 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 61 (7d8 + 30) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. In addition, Gremorly regains 9 (2d8) hit points.\n\nPossession {@recharge}\n\nOne Humanoid Gremorly can see within 5 feet of himself must succeed on a 15 Charisma saving throw or be possessed by him; Gremorly disappears, and the target has the incapacitated condition and loses control of its body. Gremorly can't be targeted by any attack, spell, or other effect, except ones that turn Undead, and he retains his alignment, Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, and immunity to the charmed and frightened conditions. He otherwise uses the target's game statistics, but Gremorly doesn't gain access to the target's knowledge, class features, or proficiencies.\n\nThe possession lasts until the target drops to 0 hit points, Gremorly ends it as a bonus action, or Gremorly is turned or forced out by an effect like the Dispel Evil and Good spell. When the possession ends, Gremorly reappears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the target. The target is immune to this Possession for 24 hours after succeeding on the saving throw or after the possession ends.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEthereal Step {@recharge 4}\n\nGremorly teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space he can see."},
  ["item.grenade-launcher.dmg2014"]={title="Grenade Launcher",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\nRaridade: none\n\n{#itemEntry Grenade|DMG"},
  ["item.grenade-launcher.xdmg2024"]={title="Grenade Launcher",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nRaridade: none\n\n{#itemEntry Grenade|XDMG"},
  ["creature.grenl.tftyp2014"]={title="Grenl",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 10 (3d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe goblin can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 4, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 4, range 80/320 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.grick.mm2014"]={title="Grick",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nStone Camouflage\n\nThe grick has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grick makes one attack with its tentacles. If that attack hits, the grick can make one beak attack against the same target.\n\nTentacles\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.grick.xmm2024"]={title="Grick",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 158\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 54 (12d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grick makes one Beak attack and one Tentacles attack.\n\nBeak\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h9 (2d6 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\nTentacles\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d10 + 2) Slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 12) from all four tentacles."},
  ["creature.grick-alpha.mm2014"]={title="Grick Alpha",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 4 | WIS 14 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nStone Camouflage\n\nThe grick has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grick makes two attacks: one with its tail and one with its tentacles. If it hits with its tentacles, the grick can make one beak attack against the same target.\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nTentacles\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (4d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.grick-ancient.xmm2024"]={title="Grick Ancient",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 158\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 135 (18d10 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 4 | WIS 14 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grick makes one Beak attack, one Slam attack, and one Tentacles attack.\n\nBeak\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h22 (4d8 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nSlam\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h7 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nTentacles\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h15 (2d10 + 4) Slashing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from all four tentacles."},
  ["creature.griffin.psx2014"]={title="Griffin",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.griffin-type-1.psz2014"]={title="Griffin (Type 1)",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.griffin-type-2.psz2014"]={title="Griffin (Type 2)",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.griffon.mm2014"]={title="Griffon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 174\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 59 (7d10 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Sight\n\nThe griffon has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe griffon makes two attacks: one with its beak and one with its claws.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.griffon.xmm2024"]={title="Griffon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 159\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 59 (7d10 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe griffon makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from both of the griffon's front claws."},
  ["creature.griffon-cavalry-rider.wdh2014"]={title="Griffon Cavalry Rider",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLance\n\nmw 4 to hit (with disadvantage against a target within 5 ft.), reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d12 + 2) piercing damage, or 11 (1d12 + 5) piercing damage while mounted.\n\nDagger\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage. Or Ranged Weapon Attack: 4 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nFeather Fall\n\nThe rider wears a magic ring with which it can cast the feather fall spell on itself once as a reaction to falling. After the spell is cast, the ring becomes nonmagical."},
  ["creature.grim-champion-of-bloodshed.bmt2014"]={title="Grim Champion of Bloodshed",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 161\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 280 (33d8 + 132)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 10 | WIS 17 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the champion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes four Blazing Morningstar attacks. It can replace one of these attacks with Blade Storm, if available.\n\nBlazing Morningstar\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) fire damage.\n\nBlade Storm {@recharge 5}\n\nThe champion conjures a churning storm of spectral blades that fills a 20-foot cube centered on a point it can see within 120 feet of itself. The storm lasts until the start of the champion's next turn. While the storm is active, the area of the storm is difficult terrain. Whenever a creature enters the storm for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it must make a 19 Dexterity saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) slashing damage on a failed saving throw, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFurious Pursuit\n\nThe champion moves up to its speed or commands its mount to move up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nInduce Violence\n\nThe champion targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or immediately make one melee weapon attack against another creature of the champion's choice that is within the target's reach. If no creature is within the target's reach or if the target has the incapacitated condition, the target instead takes 11 (2d10) psychic damage.\n\nMenace (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe champion chooses any number of creatures it can see within 30 feet of itself. Each target must succeed on a 19 Wisdom saving throw or have the frightened condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.grim-champion-of-desolation.bmt2014"]={title="Grim Champion of Desolation",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 162\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 416 (49d8 + 196)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 23 | CON 18 | INT 12 | WIS 20 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the champion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes two Leeching Blade attacks and uses Hollow Void.\n\nLeeching Blade\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage plus 33 (6d10) cold damage, and the champion regains 10 hit points.\n\nHollow Void\n\nThe champion summons a hungering rift around a creature it can see within 120 feet of itself. The creature must make a 22 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 49 (11d8) force damage and has the stunned condition until the start of the champion's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only. If a creature is reduced to 0 hit points by this effect, the creature dies, and its body crumbles to dust.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nStep into Nothing {@recharge 4}\n\nThe champion, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, has the invisible condition and teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of itself. The champion remains invisible until the start of its next turn or immediately after it deals damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCrush\n\nThe champion unleashes a burst of crushing force on a creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The creature must succeed on a 22 Strength saving throw or take 14 (4d6) force damage and have the prone condition.\n\nFearsome Pursuit\n\nThe champion moves up to its speed or commands its mount to move up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nNullify (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe champion emits a magic wave in a 60-foot cone. Every spell of 5th level or lower ends on creatures and objects of the champion's choice in that area."},
  ["creature.grim-champion-of-pestilence.bmt2014"]={title="Grim Champion of Pestilence",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 14/17\n\nPV: 120 (16d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHalo of Pestilence\n\nThe champion is surrounded by an aura of deadly magic that takes the form of a host of glowing white insects. Each creature that starts its turn within 10 feet of the champion must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw or have the incapacitated condition until the start of its next turn, as the insects ravage its body.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the champion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes two Blight Staff attacks, two Plague Bolt attacks, or one of each.\n\nBlight Staff\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 21 (6d6) necrotic damage.\n\nPlague Bolt\n\nrs 10 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h23 (4d8 + 5) poison damage, and the target has the poisoned condition until the start of the champion's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe champion makes one Blight Staff or Plague Bolt attack.\n\nFurious Pursuit\n\nThe champion moves up to its speed or commands its mount to move up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe champion uses Spellcasting."},
  ["feature.grim-harvest.phb2014.wizard.necromancy.2"]={title="Grim Harvest",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nAt 2nd level, you gain the ability to reap life energy from creatures you kill with your spells. Once per turn when you kill one or more creatures with a spell of 1st level or higher, you regain hit points equal to twice the spell's level, or three times its level if the spell belongs to the spells. You don't gain this benefit for killing constructs or undead."},
  ["species.grimlock.dmg2014"]={title="Grimlock",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nBlindsight\n\nYou have no eyes, and cannot be blinded. You can perceive your surroundings within 30 ft., or 10 ft. while deafened. You are considered blind beyond this radius.\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nYou have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nStone Camouflage\n\nYou have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Undercommon."},
  ["creature.grimlock.mm2014"]={title="Grimlock",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 175\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 9 | WIS 8 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. or 10 ft. while deafened (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Undercommon\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlind Senses\n\nThe grimlock can't use its blindsight while deafened and unable to smell.\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe grimlock has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nStone Camouflage\n\nThe grimlock has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in rocky terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSpiked Bone Club\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.grimlock.xmm2024"]={title="Grimlock",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 9 | WIS 8 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBone Cudgel\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) Psychic damage."},
  ["item.grimoire-infinitus-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Grimoire Infinitus (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.grimoire-infinitus-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Grimoire Infinitus (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 271\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nSeveral of these spellbooks with gilded pages and silver-plated covers were created during the Age of Arcanum, but only one has been found since the Calamity ended. The book has an infinite number of pages, is three inches thick, eight inches wide, twelve inches long, and weighs three pounds.\n\nDormant\n\nMost of the book is blank, but the following spells are recorded in the first pages of the tome: alarm, antimagic field, Bigby's hand, blight, charm person, confusion, control weather, create undead, detect thoughts, enlarge/reduce, fear, foresight, gaseous form, glyph of warding, legend lore, Leomund's tiny hut, mass suggestion, mislead, misty step, Mordenkainen's faithful hound, prismatic spray, ray of enfeeblement, silent image, teleport, and thunderwave.\n\nYou can use the grimoire as your spellbook, and you can scribe new spells into it as normal. When you prepare wizard spells using the grimoire, the number of wizard spells you can prepare increases by 1."},
  ["item.grimoire-infinitus-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Grimoire Infinitus (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.grimzod-gargenhale.lox2014"]={title="Grimzod Gargenhale",subtitle="Criatura - LoX - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.grinda-garloth.wdh2014"]={title="Grinda Garloth",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 65\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish, Halfling, Undercommon"},
  ["background.grinner.egw2014"]={title="Grinner",subtitle="Background - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Ballad of the Grinning Fool\n\nLike every Grinner, you know how to find a hideout. In any city of 10,000 people or more on the Menagerie Coast or in the lands of the Dwendalian Empire, you can play the \"Ballad of the Grinning Fool\" in a major tavern or inn. A member of the Golden Grin will find you and give shelter to you and any companions you vouch for. This shelter might be discontinued if it becomes too dangerous to hide you, at the DM's discretion.\n\nThis feature must be used with caution, for not all who know the ballad are your friends. Some are traitors, counterspies, or agents of tyranny.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nGrinners are trained in the art of secrecy and innuendo, and are skilled at hiding in plain sight by being the loudest and brightest person in the room. Their skills in subterfuge and combat lend themselves well to an adventuring lifestyle, and traveling with mercenaries and treasure hunters creates a convenient excuse to journey through lands bent under tyranny.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I love the spotlight. Everyone, look at me!\n\n2 | Give me a drink and I'm your friend.\n\n3 | Talk to me about yourself. I'm a hell of a listener.\n\n4 | I hate to start fights, but I love to finish them.\n\n5 | I can't sit still.\n\n6 | I'm always humming an old tune from my past.\n\n7 | When I don't have a reason to smile, I'm miserable.\n\n8 | I'm lucky like you wouldn't believe.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Revolution. Tyrants must fall, no matter the cost. (Chaotic)\n\n2 | Compassion. The only way to make a better world is to perform small kindnesses. (Good)\n\n3 | Justice. A nation built upon just foundations will uphold freedom for all. (Law)\n\n4 | Expression. Music, joy, and laughter are the keys to freedom. (Good)\n\n5 | Self-Determination. People should be free to do as they please. (Chaotic)\n\n6 | Vigilance. A free people must be carefully taught, lest they be misled. (Neutral)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | I lost someone important to an agent of the Dwendalian Empire. That regime will fall.\n\n2 | The first people to be hurt by this war will be the common folk. I need to protect them.\n\n3 | Music helped me through a dark time in my life. Now, I'll use music to change the world.\n\n4 | I will be known as the greatest spy who ever lived.\n\n5 | All life is precious to me. I know I can change the world without taking a humanoid life.\n\n6 | The elite in their ivory towers don't understand how we suffer. I intend to show them.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | I've never lied once in my life. What? No, I'm not crossing my fingers!\n\n2 | I do everything big! Subtlety? I don't know the meaning of subtlety! Oh, that's a problem?\n\n3 | Being a spy in wartime is painful. I've seen so much suffering, I think I'm losing my mind.\n\n4 | I can't focus on my mission. I just want to carouse and sing and play!\n\n5 | Yeah, that's my name. Yeah, I'm a Grinner spy. Who cares about staying undercover?\n\n6 | I can't afford to trust anyone. Not. Anyone."},
  ["creature.grinning-cat.bgg2014"]={title="Grinning Cat",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 45 (7d10 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 13 | INT 15 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe grinning cat has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) slashing damage. If the grinning cat was invisible before it attacked, the target must succeed on a 12 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition. If the target has the prone condition, the cat can make a Bite attack against it as a bonus action.\n\nFade Away\n\nThe grinning cat magically becomes invisible for 1 hour or until it attacks, gradually fading away over the course of its turn. It can choose to leave part of its body visible, such as its tail, its head, or its grinning mouth. Any equipment the cat wears or carries is invisible with it.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nFade Back\n\nThe grinning cat becomes visible or makes part of its body visible. Any equipment the cat wears or carries on a visible part of its body also becomes visible.\n\nGrinning Step\n\nThe grinning cat teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.grippli-warrior.cm2014"]={title="Grippli Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 99\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Grippli plus one other language (usually Common, Draconic, or Primordial)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe grippli can hold its breath for 20 minutes.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe grippli can leap 30 feet horizontally or 20 feet vertically from a standing position.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe grippli makes one attack with its tongue. If this attack hits, the grippli can make a melee attack using its trident against the same target.\n\nTongue\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature. hThe target is grappled (escape 12). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the grippli can't grab another creature.\n\nTrident\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack, plus 2 (1d4) piercing damage if the grippli had advantage on the attack roll.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, plus 2 (1d4) piercing damage if the grippli had advantage on the attack roll."},
  ["creature.grisdelfawr.qftis2014"]={title="Grisdelfawr",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.grisha.oota2014"]={title="Grisha",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Undercommon\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nGrisha makes two attacks with his +1 flail.\n\n+1 Flail\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.groff.scc2014"]={title="Groff",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 68 (8d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 4 | WIS 13 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the groff is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the groff move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the groff isn't an ordinary moss-covered bog patch.\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe groff can hold its breath for up to 1 hour.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe groff makes one Bite attack and one Swamp Claw attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nSwamp Claw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or become engulfed by the groff. While engulfed, the target can't breathe, is restrained, and takes 10 (3d6) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. When the groff moves, the engulfed target moves with it. The groff can have only one target engulfed at a time.\n\nAn engulfed target can repeat the saving throw at the end of its turns. On a success, the target escapes and enters the nearest unoccupied space."},
  ["deity.grolantor.phb2014"]={title="Grolantor",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["creature.gromin-gorn.idrotf2014"]={title="Gromin'gorn",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 140\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.grotesque-tentacle.coa2014"]={title="Grotesque Tentacle",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 78\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0"},
  ["creature.grottenelle-stonecutter.veor2014"]={title="Grottenelle Stonecutter",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 49\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.groundling-grunt.au2014"]={title="Groundling Grunt",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 143\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 7 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 13) from one of two paws.\n\nSling\n\nr 4, range 30/120 ft. h7 (2d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nGo to Ground\n\nactTrigger The groundling is hit by an attack roll while it is on the ground. actResponse The groundling halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["creature.groundling-slayer.au2014"]={title="Groundling Slayer",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe groundling makes two attacks, using Claw or Dagger in any combination.\n\nClaw\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 13) from one of two paws.\n\nDagger\n\nm,r 5, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nGo to Ground\n\nactTrigger The groundling is hit by an attack roll while it is on the ground. actResponse The groundling halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["creature.groundling-stalker.au2014"]={title="Groundling Stalker",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 13) from one of two paws.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nr 5, range 100/400 ft. h14 (2d10 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nGo to Ground\n\nactTrigger The groundling is hit by an attack roll while it is on the ground. actResponse The groundling halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["feature.group-recovery.frhof2014.fighter.banneret.3"]={title="Group Recovery",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nWhen you use your Second Wind to regain XPHB, you can choose a number of allies within a 30-foot XPHB originating from yourself, up to a number of allies equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one). Each of those allies regains XPHB equal to 1d4 plus your Fighter level. Once you use this ability, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["item.grovelthrash-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Grovelthrash (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.grovelthrash-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Grovelthrash (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 275\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nCrafted from a single piece of obsidian, this warhammer of Torog hums with magical energy and is carved with the images of faces screaming in pain.\n\nSentience\n\nGrovelthrash is a sentient neutral evil weapon with an Intelligence of 18, a Wisdom of 15, and a Charisma of 19. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\n\nThe weapon communicates telepathically with its wielder and can speak, read, and understand Abyssal, Common, and Infernal.\n\nPersonality\n\nA covetous ultroloth named Ciria lives within Grovelthrash. The weapon values material possessions and doling out pain. It compliments its wielder whenever they claim treasure and takes pleasure in harming others.\n\nDormant\n\nThe warhammer grants the following benefits in its dormant state:\n\n• You can speak, read, and write Abyssal and Infernal.\n\n• You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. When you hit with an attack using this warhammer, you can deal an extra 2d6 bludgeoning damage to the target. If you do, you take 1d6 psychic damage. The warhammer deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n• While holding this weapon, you have advantage on Wisdom (Insight) checks made to discern a lie spoken in a language you understand.\n\nBetrayer Artifact Properties\n\nThe Arms of the Betrayers advance in power in the same manner as the Vestiges of Divergence. In its dormant state, each of these artifacts has one dmg property and one dmg property. When the artifact attains an awakened state, it gains an additional dmg property and an additional dmg property. When the item reaches its exalted state, it gains a dmg property. See \"Artifact Properties\" in chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for more information."},
  ["item.grovelthrash-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Grovelthrash (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.grum-shar.wdh2014"]={title="Grum'shar",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Orc\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRelentless Endurance\n\nWhen reduced to 0 hit points, Grum'shar drops to 1 hit point instead. He can only do this once per long rest.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) piercing damage. Or Ranged Weapon Attack: 2 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) piercing damage."},
  ["deity.grumbar.scag2014"]={title="Grumbar",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21"},
  ["creature.grumink-the-renegade.pota2014"]={title="Grumink the Renegade",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft."},
  ["creature.grung.mpmm2014"]={title="Grung",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25, climb: 25\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Grung\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe grung can breathe air and water.\n\nPoisonous Skin\n\nAny creature that grapples the grung or otherwise comes into direct contact with the grung's skin must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1 minute. A poisoned creature no longer in direct contact with the grung can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe grung's long jump is up to 25 feet and its high jump is up to 15 feet, with or without a running start.\n\nWater Dependency\n\nIf the grung isn't immersed in water for at least 1 hour during a day, it suffers 1 level of exhaustion at the end of that day. The grung can recover from this exhaustion only through magic or by immersing itself in water for at least 1 hour.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage plus 5 (2d4) poison damage."},
  ["species.grung.oga2014"]={title="Grung",subtitle="Especie - OGA - 2014",body="Pagina: 4\n\nAge\n\nGrungs mature to adulthood in a single year, but have been known to live up to 50 years.\n\nAlignment\n\nMost grungs are lawful, having been raised in a strict caste system. They tend toward evil as well, coming from a culture where social advancement occurs rarely, and most often because another member of your army has died and there is no one else of that caste to fill the vacancy.\n\nSize\n\nGrungs stand between 2½ and 3½ feet tall and average about 30 pounds. Your size is Small.\n\nArboreal Alertness\n\nYou have proficiency in the Perception skill.\n\nAmphibious\n\nYou can breathe air and water.\n\nPoison Immunity\n\nYou're immune to poison damage and the poisoned condition.\n\nPoisonous Skin\n\nAny creature that grapples you or otherwise comes into direct contact with your skin must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1 minute. A poisoned creature no longer in direct contact with you can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nYou can also apply this poison to any piercing weapon as part of an attack with that weapon, though when you hit the poison reacts differently. The target must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or take 2d4 poison damage.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nYour long jump is up to 25 feet and your high jump is up to 15 feet, with or without a running start.\n\nWater Dependency\n\nIf you fail to immerse yourself in water for at least 1 hour during a day, you suffer one level of exhaustion at the end of that day. You can only recover from this exhaustion through magic or by immersing yourself in water for at least 1 hour.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Grung."},
